{"jobs":[{"id":"c21e6033-02c8-4bba-8607-97e0934e71d1","title":"Managing Director/Director, Relationship Management, Wealth Advisory","department":"Relationship Management","team":"Relationship Management","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Palo Alto (On-Site)","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-02-24T20:31:25.995+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":false,"workplaceType":"OnSite","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Palo Alto"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/allocate/c21e6033-02c8-4bba-8607-97e0934e71d1","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/allocate/c21e6033-02c8-4bba-8607-97e0934e71d1/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are seeking a Managing Director and/or Director of Relationship Management to deepen and expand our engagement with wealth advisory firms. This individual will be responsible for managing and growing relationships with RIAs, multi-family offices, and private wealth managers, ensuring they leverage Allocate's platform to enhance their private market allocations. The ideal candidate has a deep understanding of private markets, a proven ability to build trusted partnerships with sophisticated wealth advisors, and a strong passion for building a next-generation private markets technology company.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>Responsibilities</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop and manage relationships with RIAs, multi-family offices, and independent wealth managers, with a primary focus on establishing and growing relationships with new wealth advisory firms.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as a trusted advisor, educating firms on private market strategies and the benefits of Allocate's platform and suite of investment and technology solutions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with advisory teams to structure private market portfolios that align with their clients' investment objectives.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive engagement and platform adoption by delivering high-touch relationship management, training, and thought leadership.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Act as a subject matter expert on venture capital, private equity, co-investments, and other alternative investments, guiding advisors on manager selection, fund structures, and portfolio construction.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide market intelligence, feedback, and insights to internal teams to enhance our offerings and client experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Represent Allocate at industry conferences, roundtables, and client events to strengthen brand presence and thought leadership.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Qualifications &amp; Experience</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">8+ years of experience in relationship management, sales, or advisory roles within private markets, asset management, or wealth management</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Established network of RIAs, multi-family offices, and private wealth advisors, with a specific focus on HNW/UHNW wealth advisory firms.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep understanding of private market investments, including venture capital, private equity, co-investments, and alternative asset allocation strategies.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong knowledge and passion for delivering technology-driven solutions, with previous technology sales experience strongly preferred.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with investment platforms, fund structures, and a range of alternative investment vehicles.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven ability to build and maintain relationships with senior-level decision-makers at wealth advisory firms.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication and presentation skills, with an ability to simplify complex investment concepts for different audiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strategic and consultative approach to client engagement, with a focus on long-term partnerships.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to work independently; travel as needed within the region.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Essential Values &amp; Culture</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Providing our clients with a world-class experience</strong></em> is our number one priority. We obsessively search for ways to improve the experience for our clients and partners. This requires extraordinary response times, proactivity, and ensuring that everything we do, from product strategy to offline communications is a top-tier client experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Challenge convention:</strong></em> Instead of detailing all the reasons why an idea may not work, we constantly question things to determine how a viable idea may be put into motion.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Commitment to continuous improvement:</strong></em> We find ways to personally scale each day by pushing ourselves up the learning curve.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Meritocracy, not politics:</strong></em> We place the utmost value on results and rewards through merit, not reward actions driven by political agendas or behavior.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Civil Discourse is embraced:</strong></em> We believe open, intellectually curious conversations are required to consistently arrive at the best decisions. Respect is paramount in our dealings with one another, but our mission is always to get the right answer collectively, not to be right.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Why join Allocate?</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be part of a high-growth fintech firm revolutionizing access to private markets.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work alongside a talented team of investment professionals, technologists, and industry leaders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Opportunity to shape the future of private market investing for wealth advisory firms and their clients.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Competitive compensation package, including base salary, performance incentives, and equity participation</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Additional Details</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Location: New York City or Menlo Park, CA (must be able to work from our New York City or Menlo Park office 3-4 days a week or as needed)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Salary Range: $150,000 - $220,000. The actual salary will be determined based on the candidate's experience, location, skills, training, certifications and education, and other relevant qualifications specific to the role, as well as internal equity and market data. Total compensation may include discretionary performance-based bonuses based on individual, team, and company performance factors, and equity.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Benefits: Medical, dental, vision, responsible time off (RTO), and 401K</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Employment: Full-time</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The role will be subject to Allocate's Code of Ethics and related compliance obligations of Allocate.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">In compliance with federal law, all persons hired will be required to verify identity and eligibility to work in the United States and to complete the required employment eligibility verification form upon hire. Must have legal authorization to work in the U.S. now and in the future without visa sponsorship.</p>","descriptionPlain":"We are seeking a Managing Director and/or Director of Relationship Management to deepen and expand our engagement with wealth advisory firms. This individual will be responsible for managing and growing relationships with RIAs, multi-family offices, and private wealth managers, ensuring they leverage Allocate's platform to enhance their private market allocations. The ideal candidate has a deep understanding of private markets, a proven ability to build trusted partnerships with sophisticated wealth advisors, and a strong passion for building a next-generation private markets technology company.\n\n \n\n\nRESPONSIBILITIES\n\n - Develop and manage relationships with RIAs, multi-family offices, and independent wealth managers, with a primary focus on establishing and growing relationships with new wealth advisory firms.\n\n - Serve as a trusted advisor, educating firms on private market strategies and the benefits of Allocate's platform and suite of investment and technology solutions.\n\n - Partner with advisory teams to structure private market portfolios that align with their clients' investment objectives.\n\n - Drive engagement and platform adoption by delivering high-touch relationship management, training, and thought leadership.\n\n - Act as a subject matter expert on venture capital, private equity, co-investments, and other alternative investments, guiding advisors on manager selection, fund structures, and portfolio construction.\n\n - Provide market intelligence, feedback, and insights to internal teams to enhance our offerings and client experience.\n\n - Represent Allocate at industry conferences, roundtables, and client events to strengthen brand presence and thought leadership.\n\n\nQUALIFICATIONS & EXPERIENCE\n\n - 8+ years of experience in relationship management, sales, or advisory roles within private markets, asset management, or wealth management\n\n - Established network of RIAs, multi-family offices, and private wealth advisors, with a specific focus on HNW/UHNW wealth advisory firms.\n\n - Deep understanding of private market investments, including venture capital, private equity, co-investments, and alternative asset allocation strategies.\n\n - Strong knowledge and passion for delivering technology-driven solutions, with previous technology sales experience strongly preferred.\n\n - Experience working with investment platforms, fund structures, and a range of alternative investment vehicles.\n\n - Proven ability to build and maintain relationships with senior-level decision-makers at wealth advisory firms.\n\n - Strong communication and presentation skills, with an ability to simplify complex investment concepts for different audiences.\n\n - Strategic and consultative approach to client engagement, with a focus on long-term partnerships.\n\n - Ability to work independently; travel as needed within the region.\n\n\nESSENTIAL VALUES & CULTURE\n\n - Providing our clients with a world-class experience is our number one priority. We obsessively search for ways to improve the experience for our clients and partners. This requires extraordinary response times, proactivity, and ensuring that everything we do, from product strategy to offline communications is a top-tier client experience.\n\n - Challenge convention: Instead of detailing all the reasons why an idea may not work, we constantly question things to determine how a viable idea may be put into motion.\n\n - Commitment to continuous improvement: We find ways to personally scale each day by pushing ourselves up the learning curve.\n\n - Meritocracy, not politics: We place the utmost value on results and rewards through merit, not reward actions driven by political agendas or behavior.\n\n - Civil Discourse is embraced: We believe open, intellectually curious conversations are required to consistently arrive at the best decisions. Respect is paramount in our dealings with one another, but our mission is always to get the right answer collectively, not to be right.\n\n\nWHY JOIN ALLOCATE?\n\n - Be part of a high-growth fintech firm revolutionizing access to private markets.\n\n - Work alongside a talented team of investment professionals, technologists, and industry leaders.\n\n - Opportunity to shape the future of private market investing for wealth advisory firms and their clients.\n\n - Competitive compensation package, including base salary, performance incentives, and equity participation\n\n\nADDITIONAL DETAILS\n\n - Location: New York City or Menlo Park, CA (must be able to work from our New York City or Menlo Park office 3-4 days a week or as needed)\n\n - Salary Range: $150,000 - $220,000. The actual salary will be determined based on the candidate's experience, location, skills, training, certifications and education, and other relevant qualifications specific to the role, as well as internal equity and market data. Total compensation may include discretionary performance-based bonuses based on individual, team, and company performance factors, and equity.\n\n - Benefits: Medical, dental, vision, responsible time off (RTO), and 401K\n\n - Employment: Full-time\n\n - The role will be subject to Allocate's Code of Ethics and related compliance obligations of Allocate.\n\nIn compliance with federal law, all persons hired will be required to verify identity and eligibility to work in the United States and to complete the required employment eligibility verification form upon hire. Must have legal authorization to work in the U.S. now and in the future without visa sponsorship.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$150K – $220K","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$150K - $220K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"dc542796-d99b-4353-b9b2-d7ff647e1f37","tierSummary":"$150K – $220K","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"6dfbbc1c-35d9-4977-852b-baee9b2223db","summary":"$150K – $220K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":150000,"maxValue":220000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":150000,"maxValue":220000}]}},{"id":"7d63e99a-5867-44b2-a0ab-753e3e4e8ba4","title":"Sr. Director, Limited Partner Relations & Servicing","department":"Investor Services","team":"Investor Services","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Palo Alto (On-Site)","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-02-24T16:33:21.655+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":false,"workplaceType":"OnSite","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Palo Alto"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/allocate/7d63e99a-5867-44b2-a0ab-753e3e4e8ba4","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/allocate/7d63e99a-5867-44b2-a0ab-753e3e4e8ba4/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>About the role</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As Director of Limited Partner Relations &amp; Servicing, you will build and lead the team that services Allocate's 4,000+ investors across 150+ funds. This team handles everything investors need: onboarding to the platform, subscription documents, KYC coordination, custodian issues, ongoing platform questions, and general inquiries. You are accountable for response times, accuracy, and investor satisfaction as the business continues to scale.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a management role, and you will be required to develop and run a team that can handle high volume and complexity without you being the bottleneck. You will build the processes and systems that let your team operate independently while maintaining quality and speed.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role requires someone who has managed and scaled teams through growth—not just operated as a strong individual contributor. You will partner closely with Relationship Management, Investment Research, Product, Legal, Finance, and Engineering, but your primary accountability is leading your team and running investor servicing operations.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Responsibilities include (but are not limited to):</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Team Leadership &amp; Management</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage a team of investor services professionals—set clear expectations, give direct feedback, develop people, and hire when needed</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build a team that doesn't need you to answer every question; your job is to scale through people, not just personal capacity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Handle performance management, coaching, and team development as the business grows</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Investor Servicing Operations</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the full investor lifecycle: onboarding new RIAs to the platform, handling subscription document questions, coordinating KYC, resolving custodian issues, and answering ongoing investor inquiries</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as the escalation point for complex or high-stakes investor situations—handle them directly or coach your team through resolution</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ensure fast, accurate responses that maintain investor trust and satisfaction</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will be asked to serve as the primary point of client servicing for Allocate’s largest enterprise clients</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Process &amp; Systems Building</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build scalable processes that work as we grow from 4,000 to 8,000+ investors—identify what's breaking and fix it before it becomes a crisis</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track the metrics that matter: response times, resolution rates, investor satisfaction, team capacity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Implement systems and tools that make your team more effective without degrading quality</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Cross-Functional Partnership</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work with Product, Legal, Finance, and Engineering on anything that impacts investor experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Relationship Management to ensure RMs trust that escalations get resolved quickly and correctly</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Push for changes that make your team's job easier or improve the investor experience</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Qualifications</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">7+ years in alternative asset management, private wealth management, or adjacent financial services environments with exposure to RIAs, family offices, fund structures, subscription documents, custodians, and KYC processes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven experience managing and scaling teams through periods of growth—you've built or run teams, know how to hire and develop people, and have handled the messy middle of scaling when old processes break</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Operational mindset: you see broken processes and fix them, identify bottlenecks and remove them, and bring structure to ambiguity without needing perfect systems to get started</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">High responsiveness and attention to detail—you hold yourself and your team to the standard that investors expect, fast, accurate answers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong judgment and communication skills—you can handle difficult conversations with investors, partners, and internal teams clearly, directly, and professionally</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Technical fluency with CRMs, operational tools, and basic data tracking to evaluate and implement systems that improve team effectiveness</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>This role is NOT a fit if:</strong> You are primarily an individual contributor who enjoys client servicing but hasn't managed or led teams. You will do some of that work, but your primary job is leading people and running operations.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Essential Values &amp; Culture</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Providing our clients with a world-class experience is our number one priority. This role is critical to how our values show up for investors every day. We obsessively search for ways to improve the experience for our clients and partners, requiring extraordinary response times, proactivity, and a relentless focus on quality across everything we do.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Challenge convention:</strong> We question assumptions and focus on how ideas can be put into motion.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Commitment to continuous improvement:</strong> We push ourselves up the learning curve and expect the same from our systems and processes.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Meritocracy, not politics: </strong>Results matter more than posturing.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Civil discourse is embraced:</strong> Respectful, intellectually curious debate is essential to making the best decisions collectively.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>Additional Details</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location: </strong>Palo Alto, CA<br /><strong>Salary Range:</strong> $190–230k base salary + equity<br />May qualify for a discretionary bonus if employed and in good standing at the end of the fiscal year<br /><strong>Benefits: </strong>Medical, dental, vision, responsible time off (RTO), 401k<br /><strong>Employment:</strong> Full-time</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role will be subject to Allocate's Code of Ethics and related compliance obligations.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The base pay offered will be determined based on the candidate's experience, location, skills, training, certifications, education, internal equity, and market data. Total compensation may also include a discretionary performance-based bonus. We do not anticipate that candidates hired will begin at the top of the range, though this may occur on a case-by-case basis.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT THE ROLE\n\nAs Director of Limited Partner Relations & Servicing, you will build and lead the team that services Allocate's 4,000+ investors across 150+ funds. This team handles everything investors need: onboarding to the platform, subscription documents, KYC coordination, custodian issues, ongoing platform questions, and general inquiries. You are accountable for response times, accuracy, and investor satisfaction as the business continues to scale.\n\nThis is a management role, and you will be required to develop and run a team that can handle high volume and complexity without you being the bottleneck. You will build the processes and systems that let your team operate independently while maintaining quality and speed.\n\nThis role requires someone who has managed and scaled teams through growth—not just operated as a strong individual contributor. You will partner closely with Relationship Management, Investment Research, Product, Legal, Finance, and Engineering, but your primary accountability is leading your team and running investor servicing operations.\n\n\n\n\nRESPONSIBILITIES INCLUDE (BUT ARE NOT LIMITED TO):\n\nTeam Leadership & Management\n\n - Manage a team of investor services professionals—set clear expectations, give direct feedback, develop people, and hire when needed\n\n - Build a team that doesn't need you to answer every question; your job is to scale through people, not just personal capacity\n\n - Handle performance management, coaching, and team development as the business grows\n\nInvestor Servicing Operations\n\n - Own the full investor lifecycle: onboarding new RIAs to the platform, handling subscription document questions, coordinating KYC, resolving custodian issues, and answering ongoing investor inquiries\n\n - Serve as the escalation point for complex or high-stakes investor situations—handle them directly or coach your team through resolution\n\n - Ensure fast, accurate responses that maintain investor trust and satisfaction\n\n - You will be asked to serve as the primary point of client servicing for Allocate’s largest enterprise clients\n\nProcess & Systems Building\n\n - Build scalable processes that work as we grow from 4,000 to 8,000+ investors—identify what's breaking and fix it before it becomes a crisis\n\n - Track the metrics that matter: response times, resolution rates, investor satisfaction, team capacity\n\n - Implement systems and tools that make your team more effective without degrading quality\n\nCross-Functional Partnership\n\n - Work with Product, Legal, Finance, and Engineering on anything that impacts investor experience\n\n - Partner with Relationship Management to ensure RMs trust that escalations get resolved quickly and correctly\n\n - Push for changes that make your team's job easier or improve the investor experience\n\nQualifications\n\n - 7+ years in alternative asset management, private wealth management, or adjacent financial services environments with exposure to RIAs, family offices, fund structures, subscription documents, custodians, and KYC processes\n\n - Proven experience managing and scaling teams through periods of growth—you've built or run teams, know how to hire and develop people, and have handled the messy middle of scaling when old processes break\n\n - Operational mindset: you see broken processes and fix them, identify bottlenecks and remove them, and bring structure to ambiguity without needing perfect systems to get started\n\n - High responsiveness and attention to detail—you hold yourself and your team to the standard that investors expect, fast, accurate answers\n\n - Strong judgment and communication skills—you can handle difficult conversations with investors, partners, and internal teams clearly, directly, and professionally\n\n - Technical fluency with CRMs, operational tools, and basic data tracking to evaluate and implement systems that improve team effectiveness\n\nThis role is NOT a fit if: You are primarily an individual contributor who enjoys client servicing but hasn't managed or led teams. You will do some of that work, but your primary job is leading people and running operations.\n\nEssential Values & Culture\n\nProviding our clients with a world-class experience is our number one priority. This role is critical to how our values show up for investors every day. We obsessively search for ways to improve the experience for our clients and partners, requiring extraordinary response times, proactivity, and a relentless focus on quality across everything we do.\n\nChallenge convention: We question assumptions and focus on how ideas can be put into motion.\n\nCommitment to continuous improvement: We push ourselves up the learning curve and expect the same from our systems and processes.\n\nMeritocracy, not politics: Results matter more than posturing.\n\nCivil discourse is embraced: Respectful, intellectually curious debate is essential to making the best decisions collectively.\n\n \n\n\nADDITIONAL DETAILS\n\nLocation: Palo Alto, CA\nSalary Range: $190–230k base salary + equity\nMay qualify for a discretionary bonus if employed and in good standing at the end of the fiscal year\nBenefits: Medical, dental, vision, responsible time off (RTO), 401k\nEmployment: Full-time\n\nThis role will be subject to Allocate's Code of Ethics and related compliance obligations.\n\nThe base pay offered will be determined based on the candidate's experience, location, skills, training, certifications, education, internal equity, and market data. Total compensation may also include a discretionary performance-based bonus. We do not anticipate that candidates hired will begin at the top of the range, though this may occur on a case-by-case basis.\n\n ","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$190K – $230K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$190K - $230K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"d1f1e56c-cce0-4e9c-8a3a-a38896ba7e43","tierSummary":"$190K – $230K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"c566c976-1adb-4c85-9113-b7c9253fb4ee","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"c3d4d2b0-9b9d-4c2e-8511-8603ef2226a8","summary":"$190K – $230K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":190000,"maxValue":230000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":190000,"maxValue":230000}]}},{"id":"374643d3-6635-432a-b34a-4b7d78878c08","title":"Senior Director/ Director, RIA Relationship Management (West Coast)","department":"Relationship Management","team":"Relationship Management","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Palo Alto Office (Hybrid)","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"Palo Alto (On-Site)","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Palo Alto"}}}],"publishedAt":"2026-04-15T14:46:31.105+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Palo Alto"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/allocate/374643d3-6635-432a-b34a-4b7d78878c08","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/allocate/374643d3-6635-432a-b34a-4b7d78878c08/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>The Role</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are hiring a Director / Senior Director, RIA Relationship Management to help lead Allocate’s growth with wealth advisory firms, specifically focused on [West Coast, Midwest, East Coast] RIAs.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role focuses exclusively on RIAs and wealth advisory firms, partnering with their CIOs, investment teams, and core operating partners, to help them build programmatic private markets portfolios using Allocate’s platform.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will operate at the intersection of investment expertise, consultative sales, and strategic relationship building, helping build the future of private markets.</p><h2><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build trusted relationships with CIOs, investment committees, and senior leadership at leading RIAs to help scale their private markets programs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive adoption of Allocate’s platform across curated investment opportunities (from venture and growth to private equity and private credit), white label fund solutions, and Allocate Insights, focusing on driving adoption and revenue growth</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead the full relationship lifecycle from initial introduction to long-term partnership</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner closely with the investment, product, and operations teams to deliver exceptional client outcomes, creating a consistent feedback loop between clients and product innovation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be a leader out in the field for Allocate, representing Allocate at industry events and key client gatherings</p></li></ul><h2><strong>What We’re Looking For</strong></h2><h3><strong>Qualifications</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">7–10+ years of experience in relationship management, focused on RIAs and wealth advisory firms</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional relationship-building ability with senior decision makers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to explain complex investment strategies clearly</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Background specifically in alternatives, technology sales, or a combination of both (Preference for strong technology background and interest)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience, knowledge and interest in sophisticated alternatives offerings, from venture growth, and private equity to co-investments and secondaries opportunities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record of sourcing and closing complex deals</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strategic account development mindset</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">High degree of self-direction and ownership</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort operating in a fast-moving, entrepreneurial environment</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Why Join Allocate</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work directly with some of the most sophisticated platforms in wealth management</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help build the infrastructure powering private markets in the RIA channel</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Join a team of builders focused on client experience, operational rigor, and problem solving</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Shape how the next generation of wealth platforms invest in private markets</p></li></ul>","descriptionPlain":"THE ROLE\n\nWe are hiring a Director / Senior Director, RIA Relationship Management to help lead Allocate’s growth with wealth advisory firms, specifically focused on [West Coast, Midwest, East Coast] RIAs.\n\nThis role focuses exclusively on RIAs and wealth advisory firms, partnering with their CIOs, investment teams, and core operating partners, to help them build programmatic private markets portfolios using Allocate’s platform.\n\nYou will operate at the intersection of investment expertise, consultative sales, and strategic relationship building, helping build the future of private markets.\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Build trusted relationships with CIOs, investment committees, and senior leadership at leading RIAs to help scale their private markets programs\n\n - Drive adoption of Allocate’s platform across curated investment opportunities (from venture and growth to private equity and private credit), white label fund solutions, and Allocate Insights, focusing on driving adoption and revenue growth\n\n - Lead the full relationship lifecycle from initial introduction to long-term partnership\n\n - Partner closely with the investment, product, and operations teams to deliver exceptional client outcomes, creating a consistent feedback loop between clients and product innovation\n\n - Be a leader out in the field for Allocate, representing Allocate at industry events and key client gatherings\n\n\nWHAT WE’RE LOOKING FOR\n\n\nQUALIFICATIONS\n\n - 7–10+ years of experience in relationship management, focused on RIAs and wealth advisory firms\n\n - Exceptional relationship-building ability with senior decision makers\n\n - Ability to explain complex investment strategies clearly\n\n - Background specifically in alternatives, technology sales, or a combination of both (Preference for strong technology background and interest)\n\n - Experience, knowledge and interest in sophisticated alternatives offerings, from venture growth, and private equity to co-investments and secondaries opportunities\n\n - Track record of sourcing and closing complex deals\n\n - Strategic account development mindset\n\n - High degree of self-direction and ownership\n\n - Comfort operating in a fast-moving, entrepreneurial environment\n\n\n\n\nWHY JOIN ALLOCATE\n\n - Work directly with some of the most sophisticated platforms in wealth management\n\n - Help build the infrastructure powering private markets in the RIA channel\n\n - Join a team of builders focused on client experience, operational rigor, and problem solving\n\n - Shape how the next generation of wealth platforms invest in private markets","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$150K – $200K • Offers Equity • Offers Commission","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$150K - $200K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"8603c626-1813-4272-a81a-73c19c761fde","tierSummary":"$150K – $200K • Offers Equity • Offers Commission","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"83d06ca9-09ef-466e-aa0e-e3536edc53fc","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"3aa1ce06-fe4b-49cf-aa70-facd424f4538","summary":"Offers Commission","compensationType":"Commission","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"b4f3d85e-df8f-4e30-a518-9e63fb67171f","summary":"$150K – $200K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":150000,"maxValue":200000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Commission","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":150000,"maxValue":200000}]}},{"id":"37844c02-ef2a-41b5-9c28-b9713486262c","title":"Sr. Software Engineer II - Backend (Remote)","department":"Software Engineering","team":"Software Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-04-01T19:19:10.586+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Palo Alto"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/allocate/37844c02-ef2a-41b5-9c28-b9713486262c","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/allocate/37844c02-ef2a-41b5-9c28-b9713486262c/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Allocate</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Allocate is transforming private market investing by enabling RIAs and family offices to seamlessly discover, model, and manage their private market exposure.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our platform combines curated fund and co-investment opportunities with institutional-grade infrastructure. Through a single, data-rich digital experience, clients access top-tier opportunities across venture capital, private equity, private credit, and other private asset classes—backed by powerful tracking, analytics, and administration tools.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><strong>About the Role</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Allocate is looking to add a new <strong>Senior Software Engineer II - Backend</strong> to the team! There’s a lot for us to build, and we need a developer with a broad skillset who can jump right in to help us lay the technical foundation for the company’s future.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><strong>Essential Responsibilities and Duties</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design &amp; implement new features and endpoints in backend APIs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design &amp; implement schema changes to support these new features</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in an Agile-based development environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work as part of an independent, cross-functional squad to deliver critical features for our platform</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build high-quality, scalable, and testable code that will help drive engineering maturity and efficiency</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><strong>Must Have Experience</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years of object-oriented software engineering experience (C#, Java, etc)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years of experience with SQL-based databases (Postgres ideally)</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Must understand how to design a schema that will result in a performant application (for example: when to add an index, and to which fields)</p></li></ul></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3+ years C# experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">2+ years experience developing REST APIs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficiency with Git and version control systems in general</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience with AI-assisted development tools such as Claude Code, OpenAI’s Codex, or Cursor, and a demonstrated ability to continuously evaluate and incorporate new tools into your workflow as they emerge</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Nice to Haves</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://ASP.NET\">ASP.NET</a> Web API development experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with basic ORM concepts (such as Dapper, Entity Framework, etc)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with FluentMigrator</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Docker and Docker Compose experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">AWS ECS/EKS experience</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Education</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, similar technical field of study, or equivalent practical experience</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><strong>Essential Values &amp; Culture</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Providing our clients with a world-class experience is our number one priority.</strong> We obsessively search for ways to improve the experience for our clients and partners. This requires extraordinary response times, proactivity, and ensuring that everything we do, from product strategy to offline communications is a top-tier client experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Challenge convention</strong>: Instead of detailing all the reasons why an idea may not work, we constantly question things to determine how a viable idea may be put into motion.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Commitment to continuous improvement</strong>: We find ways to personally scale each day by pushing ourselves up the learning curve.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Meritocracy, not politics</strong>: We place the utmost value on results and rewards through merit, not reward actions driven by political agendas or behavior.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Civil Discourse is embraced</strong>: We believe open, intellectually curious conversations are required to consistently arrive at the best decisions. Respect is paramount in our dealings with one another, but our mission is always to get the right answer collectively, not to be right.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Embrace technological change:</strong> We adopt tools and techniques that make us faster, smarter, and better. We stay open to innovation, especially around AI and automation, and drop outdated methods without hesitation. This includes actively integrating AI-assisted development tools into your daily workflow and staying current as the landscape evolves. Complacency kills progress, we value adaptability and curiosity.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><strong>Additional Details:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location: </strong>Fully Remote Position (All I-9 eligible candidates will be considered)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Employment:</strong> Full-time</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Seniority: </strong>Mid-level professional</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Salary: </strong>Total compensation may also include a discretionary performance-based bonus. The expected base salary range for this role is $145,000 to $175,000</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Benefits:</strong> Medical, dental, and vision. 401(k), and responsible vacation time (PTO)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Travel required for team/department offsites</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">An in-person interview may be required during the interview process</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A Broadband internet connection required</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Compliance with Allocate's Code of Ethics is a given for this role.</p></li></ul>","descriptionPlain":"About Allocate\n\nAllocate is transforming private market investing by enabling RIAs and family offices to seamlessly discover, model, and manage their private market exposure.\n\nOur platform combines curated fund and co-investment opportunities with institutional-grade infrastructure. Through a single, data-rich digital experience, clients access top-tier opportunities across venture capital, private equity, private credit, and other private asset classes—backed by powerful tracking, analytics, and administration tools.\n\n\nAbout the Role\n\nAllocate is looking to add a new Senior Software Engineer II - Backend to the team! There’s a lot for us to build, and we need a developer with a broad skillset who can jump right in to help us lay the technical foundation for the company’s future.\n\n\nEssential Responsibilities and Duties\n\n - Design & implement new features and endpoints in backend APIs\n\n - Design & implement schema changes to support these new features\n\n - Participate in an Agile-based development environment\n\n - Work as part of an independent, cross-functional squad to deliver critical features for our platform\n\n - Build high-quality, scalable, and testable code that will help drive engineering maturity and efficiency\n\n\nMust Have Experience\n\n - 5+ years of object-oriented software engineering experience (C#, Java, etc)\n\n - 5+ years of experience with SQL-based databases (Postgres ideally)\n   \n   - Must understand how to design a schema that will result in a performant application (for example: when to add an index, and to which fields)\n\n - 3+ years C# experience\n\n - 2+ years experience developing REST APIs\n\n - Proficiency with Git and version control systems in general\n\n - Hands-on experience with AI-assisted development tools such as Claude Code, OpenAI’s Codex, or Cursor, and a demonstrated ability to continuously evaluate and incorporate new tools into your workflow as they emerge\n\n\n\nNice to Haves\n\n - ASP.NET http://ASP.NET Web API development experience\n\n - Familiarity with basic ORM concepts (such as Dapper, Entity Framework, etc)\n\n - Familiarity with FluentMigrator\n\n - Docker and Docker Compose experience\n\n - AWS ECS/EKS experience\n\n\n\nEducation\n\n - Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, similar technical field of study, or equivalent practical experience\n\n\nEssential Values & Culture\n\n - Providing our clients with a world-class experience is our number one priority. We obsessively search for ways to improve the experience for our clients and partners. This requires extraordinary response times, proactivity, and ensuring that everything we do, from product strategy to offline communications is a top-tier client experience.\n\n - Challenge convention: Instead of detailing all the reasons why an idea may not work, we constantly question things to determine how a viable idea may be put into motion.\n\n - Commitment to continuous improvement: We find ways to personally scale each day by pushing ourselves up the learning curve.\n\n - Meritocracy, not politics: We place the utmost value on results and rewards through merit, not reward actions driven by political agendas or behavior.\n\n - Civil Discourse is embraced: We believe open, intellectually curious conversations are required to consistently arrive at the best decisions. Respect is paramount in our dealings with one another, but our mission is always to get the right answer collectively, not to be right.\n\n - Embrace technological change: We adopt tools and techniques that make us faster, smarter, and better. We stay open to innovation, especially around AI and automation, and drop outdated methods without hesitation. This includes actively integrating AI-assisted development tools into your daily workflow and staying current as the landscape evolves. Complacency kills progress, we value adaptability and curiosity.\n\n\nAdditional Details:\n\n - Location: Fully Remote Position (All I-9 eligible candidates will be considered)\n\n - Employment: Full-time\n\n - Seniority: Mid-level professional\n\n - Salary: Total compensation may also include a discretionary performance-based bonus. The expected base salary range for this role is $145,000 to $175,000\n\n - Benefits: Medical, dental, and vision. 401(k), and responsible vacation time (PTO)\n\n - Travel required for team/department offsites\n\n - An in-person interview may be required during the interview process\n\n - A Broadband internet connection required\n\n - Compliance with Allocate's Code of Ethics is a given for this role.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$145K – $175K","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$145K - $175K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"c224e935-1db1-4f97-be82-c2919404c647","tierSummary":"$145K – $175K","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"cdc6b3c8-c117-4f7d-8687-63c9af26a483","summary":"$145K – $175K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":145000,"maxValue":175000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":145000,"maxValue":175000}]}},{"id":"ea7672bc-1037-45ee-b9e2-06a0a7ac93f3","title":"Fund Operations Associate","department":"Fund Finance","team":"Fund Finance","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York Office (On-Site)","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-04-10T20:37:13.219+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":false,"workplaceType":"OnSite","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/allocate/ea7672bc-1037-45ee-b9e2-06a0a7ac93f3","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/allocate/ea7672bc-1037-45ee-b9e2-06a0a7ac93f3/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About the Role</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Fund Operations Associate, you will sit at the center of Allocate's fund operational and treasury infrastructure, supporting the end-to-end lifecycle of 150+ funds across the platform. This role owns the operational details that keep the Allocate funds running: capital calls, distributions, wires, lines of credit, investor data integrity, and coordination both across the Allocate team and with fund administrators, banks, and other counterparties. You are accountable for accuracy, timeliness, and the operational health of the funds on the platform.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a hands-on execution role — and one where extreme client service is non-negotiable. You will manage high-volume, detail-intensive work across multiple funds simultaneously and are expected to operate with precision and urgency. When something breaks or an investor has a question, you don't wait for someone else to solve it — you dig in, find the answer, and own the outcome. You will work closely with Client Services, Relationship Management, Legal, Fund Admin, and Product to resolve operational issues and help build the processes that let us scale.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Key Responsibilities</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Fund Lifecycle Operations</em></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Process high volumes of wires, capital calls, and distributions across the fund portfolio, ensuring data accuracy and timeliness from instruction through settlement.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate with fund administrators and custodians to reconcile positions, confirm transactions, and resolve discrepancies — following through until every break is closed.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Perform bank account reconciliations and track fund cash flows across active funds.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage the line of credit lifecycle across funds — including opening new facilities, maintaining documentation, requesting advances ahead of capital call deadlines, processing repayments, and reconciling outstanding balances.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track, calculate, and reconcile fund fees and expenses — including management fees, fund expenses, and any carried interest accruals — ensuring accuracy across fund records and investor reporting.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Client Service &amp; Problem Solving</em></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as a trusted operational partner to wealth advisors and investors — responding with urgency, communicating proactively, and following through on every request.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Client Services to resolve investor-level inquiries tied to fund operations, taking ownership of issues end-to-end rather than passing them along.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify operational friction points before they become client-facing problems, and build the fixes rather than waiting to be asked.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Process &amp; Communication</em></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Document and maintain operational procedures for core fund workflows, building repeatable systems as volume and complexity grow.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work with fund administrators, banking partners, and other service providers to ensure smooth execution across the fund lifecycle.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Qualifications</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3 - 5 years of experience in fund operations, fund administration, or a related role within alternative asset management, private equity, hedge funds, or a fund administrator.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working knowledge of private fund structures, capital call mechanics, distribution waterfalls, and investor reporting workflows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Highly organized with the ability to manage multiple deadlines across a portfolio of funds without dropping details.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Relentless problem solver who treats obstacles as puzzles, not blockers. You don't escalate without first exhausting your own options, and you follow every issue through to resolution.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record of extreme client service. You treat every advisor, investor, and internal stakeholder interaction as an opportunity to build trust, and your follow-through is a point of pride.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong reconciliation skills. You're comfortable working with large data sets, identifying breaks, and resolving them with precision.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong written and verbal communication skills. You coordinate clearly with internal teams, fund administrators, custodians, and investors under time pressure.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Systematic thinker who naturally documents processes, builds repeatable workflows, and looks for ways to create structure as volume and complexity increase.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Growth-oriented and energized by a scaling environment. You want to grow with the firm and take on more ownership as the fund count and team expand.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Active and curious AI practitioner. You are already thinking about how AI can eliminate repetitive work, surface insights faster, improve work flows, and want to implement this at work.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Why Join Us</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own a critical vertical: Lead the operational organization that powers fund delivery, with full accountability for execution outcomes across 150+ funds on the platform.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Shape the future of private markets infrastructure: Allocate is building the operating system that connects the wealth channel to institutional private markets. The operational foundation you build enables our AI-powered portfolio intelligence and the client experience we deliver every day.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Client-facing impact: This isn't a back-office role. You'll engage directly with wealth advisors and allocators who rely on our platform to manage and grow their private market portfolios — and you'll be expected to deliver an experience that's not just accurate, but exceptional.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">High ownership and visibility: Direct partnership with senior leadership, a clear mandate, and the opportunity to build a best-in-class delivery function from the ground up.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Path to broader operational leadership: As Allocate scales and additional verticals mature, this role is a natural foundation for expanded operational scope under a future COO-led structure.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborative, high-velocity culture: Join a team that moves fast, holds itself accountable, and thrives on solving hard problems — for clients and for the firm.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Additional Details</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Location: New York, NY. In-office required.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Employment: Full-time.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Salary Range: $110,000 – $125,000 base salary, plus performance-based bonus, stock options, and comprehensive benefits.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Actual salary will be determined based on the candidate's experience, location, skills, training, certifications, and education, other relevant qualifications specific to the role, and internal equity and market data. Total compensation may include equity and discretionary performance-based bonuses based on individual, team, and company performance factors.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Benefits: Medical, dental, vision, responsible time off (RTO), 401k.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p>","descriptionPlain":"About the Role\n\nAs a Fund Operations Associate, you will sit at the center of Allocate's fund operational and treasury infrastructure, supporting the end-to-end lifecycle of 150+ funds across the platform. This role owns the operational details that keep the Allocate funds running: capital calls, distributions, wires, lines of credit, investor data integrity, and coordination both across the Allocate team and with fund administrators, banks, and other counterparties. You are accountable for accuracy, timeliness, and the operational health of the funds on the platform.\n\nThis is a hands-on execution role — and one where extreme client service is non-negotiable. You will manage high-volume, detail-intensive work across multiple funds simultaneously and are expected to operate with precision and urgency. When something breaks or an investor has a question, you don't wait for someone else to solve it — you dig in, find the answer, and own the outcome. You will work closely with Client Services, Relationship Management, Legal, Fund Admin, and Product to resolve operational issues and help build the processes that let us scale.\n\n\n\nKey Responsibilities\n\nFund Lifecycle Operations\n\n - Process high volumes of wires, capital calls, and distributions across the fund portfolio, ensuring data accuracy and timeliness from instruction through settlement.\n\n - Coordinate with fund administrators and custodians to reconcile positions, confirm transactions, and resolve discrepancies — following through until every break is closed.\n\n - Perform bank account reconciliations and track fund cash flows across active funds.\n\n - Manage the line of credit lifecycle across funds — including opening new facilities, maintaining documentation, requesting advances ahead of capital call deadlines, processing repayments, and reconciling outstanding balances.\n\n - Track, calculate, and reconcile fund fees and expenses — including management fees, fund expenses, and any carried interest accruals — ensuring accuracy across fund records and investor reporting.\n\nClient Service & Problem Solving\n\n - Serve as a trusted operational partner to wealth advisors and investors — responding with urgency, communicating proactively, and following through on every request.\n\n - Partner with Client Services to resolve investor-level inquiries tied to fund operations, taking ownership of issues end-to-end rather than passing them along.\n\n - Identify operational friction points before they become client-facing problems, and build the fixes rather than waiting to be asked.\n\nProcess & Communication\n\n - Document and maintain operational procedures for core fund workflows, building repeatable systems as volume and complexity grow.\n\n - Work with fund administrators, banking partners, and other service providers to ensure smooth execution across the fund lifecycle.\n\n\n\nQualifications\n\n - 3 - 5 years of experience in fund operations, fund administration, or a related role within alternative asset management, private equity, hedge funds, or a fund administrator.\n\n - Working knowledge of private fund structures, capital call mechanics, distribution waterfalls, and investor reporting workflows.\n\n - Highly organized with the ability to manage multiple deadlines across a portfolio of funds without dropping details.\n\n - Relentless problem solver who treats obstacles as puzzles, not blockers. You don't escalate without first exhausting your own options, and you follow every issue through to resolution.\n\n - Track record of extreme client service. You treat every advisor, investor, and internal stakeholder interaction as an opportunity to build trust, and your follow-through is a point of pride.\n\n - Strong reconciliation skills. You're comfortable working with large data sets, identifying breaks, and resolving them with precision.\n\n - Strong written and verbal communication skills. You coordinate clearly with internal teams, fund administrators, custodians, and investors under time pressure.\n\n - Systematic thinker who naturally documents processes, builds repeatable workflows, and looks for ways to create structure as volume and complexity increase.\n\n - Growth-oriented and energized by a scaling environment. You want to grow with the firm and take on more ownership as the fund count and team expand.\n\n - Active and curious AI practitioner. You are already thinking about how AI can eliminate repetitive work, surface insights faster, improve work flows, and want to implement this at work.\n\n\n\nWhy Join Us\n\n - Own a critical vertical: Lead the operational organization that powers fund delivery, with full accountability for execution outcomes across 150+ funds on the platform.\n\n - Shape the future of private markets infrastructure: Allocate is building the operating system that connects the wealth channel to institutional private markets. The operational foundation you build enables our AI-powered portfolio intelligence and the client experience we deliver every day.\n\n - Client-facing impact: This isn't a back-office role. You'll engage directly with wealth advisors and allocators who rely on our platform to manage and grow their private market portfolios — and you'll be expected to deliver an experience that's not just accurate, but exceptional.\n\n - High ownership and visibility: Direct partnership with senior leadership, a clear mandate, and the opportunity to build a best-in-class delivery function from the ground up.\n\n - Path to broader operational leadership: As Allocate scales and additional verticals mature, this role is a natural foundation for expanded operational scope under a future COO-led structure.\n\n - Collaborative, high-velocity culture: Join a team that moves fast, holds itself accountable, and thrives on solving hard problems — for clients and for the firm.\n\n\n\nAdditional Details\n\n - Location: New York, NY. In-office required.\n\n - Employment: Full-time.\n\n - Salary Range: $110,000 – $125,000 base salary, plus performance-based bonus, stock options, and comprehensive benefits.\n\n - Actual salary will be determined based on the candidate's experience, location, skills, training, certifications, and education, other relevant qualifications specific to the role, and internal equity and market data. Total compensation may include equity and discretionary performance-based bonuses based on individual, team, and company performance factors.\n\n - Benefits: Medical, dental, vision, responsible time off (RTO), 401k.\n\n","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$110K – $125K","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$110K - $125K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"1a20fad6-d4a6-4d7a-ab71-173a6469f3b5","tierSummary":"$110K – $125K","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"6e3bedc4-cb04-4506-af36-9f8040c5ca9e","summary":"$110K – $125K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":110000,"maxValue":125000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":110000,"maxValue":125000}]}},{"id":"a1d89f72-f9da-4c02-84ed-576f3b9b49c5","title":"Sr. Software Engineer II - Frontend (Remote)","department":"Software Engineering","team":"Software Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-18T17:39:11.340+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Palo Alto"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/allocate/a1d89f72-f9da-4c02-84ed-576f3b9b49c5","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/allocate/a1d89f72-f9da-4c02-84ed-576f3b9b49c5/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Allocate</strong> </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Allocate is transforming private market investing by enabling RIAs and family offices to seamlessly discover, model, and manage their private market exposure. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our platform combines curated fund and co-investment opportunities with institutional-grade infrastructure. Through a single, data-rich digital experience, clients access top-tier opportunities across venture capital, private equity, private credit, and other private asset classes—backed by powerful tracking, analytics, and administration tools. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Job Description </strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Allocate is growing! There's a lot for us to build and we need someone with a broad skill set who can jump right in to help us lay the technical foundation for the company's future. We are passionate about delivering software that we are proud of while having fun developing it. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are an AI-first engineering organization. Our engineers treat AI coding tools as a core part of the daily workflow, from agentic development through code review, and we expect everyone here to push the boundaries of what those tools can do. We are equally serious about keeping a human in the loop. Engineers own every line that ships, review AI-generated work with the same rigor they would apply to a colleague’s pull request, and stay accountable for the correctness, security, and maintainability of what reaches our clients. The tools accelerate the work; the engineering judgment is still yours.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Essential Responsibilities and Duties:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Leverage the latest web technologies to develop rich but simple user experiences for new products in development </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work with our product team to iterate on designs and user experience flows </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work as part of an independent, cross-functional squad to deliver critical retail and admin portal features across the technology stack </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build reusable, testable code that will help drive engineering maturity and efficiency </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Must Have Experience: </strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5-10 years of experience building web applications </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3-5 years of experience using Vue.Js front-end framework </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">1-3 years of experience with TypeScript </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience delivering frontend software that is correct, stable, and security compliant </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Autonomy and ownership - can work without supervision </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">An AI-first development mindset: real experience shipping production code with AI agents using tools like Claude Code, Cursor, or Codex, plus informed opinions on where those tools excel and where they fall short.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Real experience shipping production code with AI agents and strong opinions on where these tools excel and where they fall short. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Attention to detail and an understanding of what makes a good user experience </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to participate in a Git-based development environment with standard work management tooling </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Basic understanding of common AWS services (S3, CloudFront, etc) and how they can be applied to solve business problems </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Entrepreneurial spirit. You are self-directed, innovative, and biased towards action in fast-paced environments. You love to build new things and thrive in ambiguity and even failure </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Nice to Haves: </strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">C#/dotnet experience </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">REST API development experience </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with agentic workflows (running async coding agents, MCP integrations, custom tooling around LLMs) </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with CI pipelines </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">DevOps experience (terraform, AWS, ECS/EKS, etc) </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Education: </strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, similar technical field of study, or equivalent amount of real-world experience </p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Essential Values &amp; Culture: </strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Providing our clients with a world-class experience is our number one priority. We obsessively search for ways to improve the experience for our clients and partners. This requires extraordinary response times, proactivity, and ensuring that everything we do, from product strategy to offline communications is a top-tier client experience. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Challenge convention: Instead of detailing all the reasons why an idea may not work, we constantly question things to determine how a viable idea may be put into motion. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Commitment to continuous improvement: We find ways to personally scale each day by pushing ourselves up the learning curve. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Meritocracy, not politics: We place the utmost value on results and rewards through merit, not reward actions driven by political agendas or behavior. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Civil Discourse is embraced: We believe open, intellectually curious conversations are required to consistently arrive at the best decisions. Respect is paramount in our dealings with one another, but our mission is always to get the right answer collectively, not to be right. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Embrace technological change: We adopt tools and techniques that make us faster, smarter, and better. We stay open to innovation, especially around AI and automation, and drop outdated methods without hesitation. Complacency kills progress, we value adaptability and curiosity. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Additional Details:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location: </strong>Fully Remote Position (All I-9 eligible candidates will be considered)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Employment:</strong> Full-time</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Seniority: </strong>Mid-level professional</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Salary: </strong>Total compensation may also include a discretionary performance-based bonus. The expected base salary range for this role is $145,000 to $175,000</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Benefits:</strong> Medical, dental, and vision. 401(k), and responsible vacation time (PTO)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Travel required for team/department offsites</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">An in-person interview may be required during the interview process</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A Broadband internet connection required</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Compliance with Allocate's Code of Ethics is a given for this role.</p></li></ul>","descriptionPlain":"About Allocate \n\nAllocate is transforming private market investing by enabling RIAs and family offices to seamlessly discover, model, and manage their private market exposure. \n\nOur platform combines curated fund and co-investment opportunities with institutional-grade infrastructure. Through a single, data-rich digital experience, clients access top-tier opportunities across venture capital, private equity, private credit, and other private asset classes—backed by powerful tracking, analytics, and administration tools. \n\n\n\nJob Description \n\nAllocate is growing! There's a lot for us to build and we need someone with a broad skill set who can jump right in to help us lay the technical foundation for the company's future. We are passionate about delivering software that we are proud of while having fun developing it. \n\nWe are an AI-first engineering organization. Our engineers treat AI coding tools as a core part of the daily workflow, from agentic development through code review, and we expect everyone here to push the boundaries of what those tools can do. We are equally serious about keeping a human in the loop. Engineers own every line that ships, review AI-generated work with the same rigor they would apply to a colleague’s pull request, and stay accountable for the correctness, security, and maintainability of what reaches our clients. The tools accelerate the work; the engineering judgment is still yours.\n\n\n\nEssential Responsibilities and Duties:\n\n - Leverage the latest web technologies to develop rich but simple user experiences for new products in development \n\n - Work with our product team to iterate on designs and user experience flows \n\n - Work as part of an independent, cross-functional squad to deliver critical retail and admin portal features across the technology stack \n\n - Build reusable, testable code that will help drive engineering maturity and efficiency \n   \n   \n\nMust Have Experience: \n\n - 5-10 years of experience building web applications \n\n - 3-5 years of experience using Vue.Js front-end framework \n\n - 1-3 years of experience with TypeScript \n\n - Experience delivering frontend software that is correct, stable, and security compliant \n\n - Autonomy and ownership - can work without supervision \n\n - An AI-first development mindset: real experience shipping production code with AI agents using tools like Claude Code, Cursor, or Codex, plus informed opinions on where those tools excel and where they fall short.\n\n - Real experience shipping production code with AI agents and strong opinions on where these tools excel and where they fall short. \n\n - Attention to detail and an understanding of what makes a good user experience \n\n - Ability to participate in a Git-based development environment with standard work management tooling \n\n - Basic understanding of common AWS services (S3, CloudFront, etc) and how they can be applied to solve business problems \n\n - Entrepreneurial spirit. You are self-directed, innovative, and biased towards action in fast-paced environments. You love to build new things and thrive in ambiguity and even failure \n   \n   \n\nNice to Haves: \n\n - C#/dotnet experience \n\n - REST API development experience \n\n - Experience with agentic workflows (running async coding agents, MCP integrations, custom tooling around LLMs) \n\n - Familiarity with CI pipelines \n\n - DevOps experience (terraform, AWS, ECS/EKS, etc) \n   \n   \n\nEducation: \n\n - Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, similar technical field of study, or equivalent amount of real-world experience \n\n\n\nEssential Values & Culture: \n\n - Providing our clients with a world-class experience is our number one priority. We obsessively search for ways to improve the experience for our clients and partners. This requires extraordinary response times, proactivity, and ensuring that everything we do, from product strategy to offline communications is a top-tier client experience. \n\n - Challenge convention: Instead of detailing all the reasons why an idea may not work, we constantly question things to determine how a viable idea may be put into motion. \n\n - Commitment to continuous improvement: We find ways to personally scale each day by pushing ourselves up the learning curve. \n\n - Meritocracy, not politics: We place the utmost value on results and rewards through merit, not reward actions driven by political agendas or behavior. \n\n - Civil Discourse is embraced: We believe open, intellectually curious conversations are required to consistently arrive at the best decisions. Respect is paramount in our dealings with one another, but our mission is always to get the right answer collectively, not to be right. \n\n - Embrace technological change: We adopt tools and techniques that make us faster, smarter, and better. We stay open to innovation, especially around AI and automation, and drop outdated methods without hesitation. Complacency kills progress, we value adaptability and curiosity. \n   \n   \n\nAdditional Details:\n\n - Location: Fully Remote Position (All I-9 eligible candidates will be considered)\n\n - Employment: Full-time\n\n - Seniority: Mid-level professional\n\n - Salary: Total compensation may also include a discretionary performance-based bonus. The expected base salary range for this role is $145,000 to $175,000\n\n - Benefits: Medical, dental, and vision. 401(k), and responsible vacation time (PTO)\n\n - Travel required for team/department offsites\n\n - An in-person interview may be required during the interview process\n\n - A Broadband internet connection required\n\n - Compliance with Allocate's Code of Ethics is a given for this role.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$145K – $175K","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$145K - $175K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"f63bcb00-ed1c-49a9-b696-8f5fafd914eb","tierSummary":"$145K – $175K","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"d0c20bd6-5206-454d-9b89-bf5a47cde6a6","summary":"$145K – $175K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":145000,"maxValue":175000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":145000,"maxValue":175000}]}},{"id":"ab86323a-5505-4451-8466-5581d277ede1","title":"Lead Product Manager, AI & Data Intelligence","department":"Product","team":"Product","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Palo Alto Office (Hybrid)","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-18T20:02:34.614+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Palo Alto"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/allocate/ab86323a-5505-4451-8466-5581d277ede1","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/allocate/ab86323a-5505-4451-8466-5581d277ede1/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>ABOUT ALLOCATE</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Allocate is building the intelligent private markets operating system for the wealth channel. We give RIAs, family offices, and institutional allocators modern infrastructure for discovering, accessing, and managing private market investments. Today that means 350+ wealth advisory firms, 1,500+ GP relationships, and over $5 billion in platform assets, and we are scaling fast.</p><h1><strong>ABOUT THE ROLE</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will own the intelligence layer of Allocate: the AI systems that turn raw private markets documents and data into insight clients trust and act on.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The raw material is some of the messiest data in finance: capital account statements, fund documents, cash flow notices, unstructured PDFs in a thousand formats. Underneath your product sits a data and extraction pipeline, built in close partnership with our Data Operations team, that turns those inputs into a structured, reliable data layer. You own that pipeline as a product, and your mandate is to make it AI-native end to end: extraction, structuring, validation, and quality handled by intelligence, not brute-force human effort.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">But the pipeline is the substrate, not the product. The product is what the intelligence does with it: surfacing patterns in investment performance and outcomes that no advisor would find by reading raw numbers, powering our Insights and Diligence products, and answering the question every end investor actually has, which is \"how is my portfolio really doing, and what should I pay attention to?\" You will decide where models create real leverage, design the systems that keep their output accurate enough to put in front of paying clients, and ship intelligence that is measurably right, not just impressive in a demo.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">That last part is the hard part, and it is why this role exists. Anyone can wire an LLM to a database. Making AI-generated analysis reliable enough that an RIA will present it to their client requires evals, monitoring, quality gates, and product judgment about when the system is good enough to ship and when it is not. We hold AI features to hard eval gates before they reach clients. You will own those gates.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is deliberately a wide seat: the pipeline, the client-facing data experience, and the intelligence on top. We keep them together because splitting them produces exactly the disconnected, half-trusted data products this industry is full of. If that scope reads as too much, this is not your role. If it reads as the whole point, keep going.</p><h1><strong>WHY THIS ROLE MATTERS</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">In private markets, data is the product. When an advisor opens a client’s portfolio, the completeness of the look-through data, the accuracy of the cash flows, and the quality of the analytics are the product experience. When the end investor asks how their portfolio is really doing, the answer is only as good as the intelligence built on top of the data.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role decides whether that answer is trustworthy and illuminating or incomplete and flat. Your impact shows up in how much manual extraction work intelligence eliminates, how confidently an RIA puts our numbers and our AI-generated analysis in front of their clients, and how often the system surfaces something about performance or outcomes the user would never have found on their own.</p><h1><strong>WHAT YOU’LL OWN</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>The AI intelligence layer. </strong>The models, agents, and systems that generate insights about investment performance and outcomes across Insights, Diligence, and other data-driven products. You decide what gets built, where AI creates leverage versus noise, and what ships.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Evals and quality gates. </strong>AI output that reaches clients passes hard, automated evaluation first. You define what \"correct\" means for each feature, build the eval and monitoring systems that enforce it, and hold the line when something is not ready. Stale, wrong, or hallucinated output in front of a client is a product failure you own.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>The AI-native data pipeline. </strong>In close partnership with Data Operations, the extraction and structuring services that turn raw documents into reliable inputs, with intelligence progressively replacing manual work. Their firsthand knowledge of what breaks is your best product input.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>The client-facing data experience. </strong>How advisors, operations teams, investment teams, and end investors access and understand portfolio data: look-through investments, cash flows, performance, and cash flow modeling. Sophisticated data made clear and intuitive, down to the column order, the tooltip, and every word of copy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Data quality as a product. </strong>Completeness, accuracy, and reliability are measured, improved, and held to a standard. These numbers go in front of clients; there is no tolerance for incorrect data, period.</p></li></ul><h1><strong>HOW YOU’LL BE MEASURED</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This seat comes with a scoreboard, and you will want one.</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Within 90 days, </strong>you own the quality metrics we stand behind with clients: eval pass rates on AI-generated output, data completeness and accuracy, and monitoring that catches problems before clients do.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Within six months, </strong>you have shipped a measurable step-change in either extraction leverage (intelligence replacing manual work per document) or client-facing insight (AI-generated analysis clients act on), with the eval evidence to prove it works.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Ongoing, </strong>you present outcomes directly to the CEO. Not status updates. Outcomes: what shipped, what moved, what you’re killing and why.</p></li></ul><h1><strong>WHO YOU ARE</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You have shipped real AI products, </strong>not just used AI tools. You have taken LLM-powered or model-driven features from prototype to production, lived the gap between a great demo and a reliable product, and built or owned the evals that closed it. You have opinions about hallucination rates, grounding, and when an agentic approach beats a deterministic one, because you have paid for the wrong answer before.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You’ve lived this industry. </strong>7+ years in product in fintech, ideally across investment data products in wealth management, asset management, or private markets. You know what RIAs, fund managers, and their investors expect: the data, the conventions, the standards.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You operate with extreme ownership. </strong>If the data is wrong, you fix it at the source. If the model output is wrong, you find out before the client does. Nobody has to ask, and nothing is someone else’s job.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You are obsessive about correctness. </strong>A single wrong cash flow, misstated return, or confidently wrong AI insight breaks trust with an advisor. You build the systems and standards that prevent it, and you will not rest until the experience is right, down to the last tooltip and word of copy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You live on client calls </strong>and treat Data Operations and client-facing teams like partners, not a ticket queue. You find the real problem and build the thing that actually solves it, rigorous enough for an investment team and intuitive enough for an end investor. You prototype with modern AI tools daily and raise that standard for everyone around you.</p></li></ul><h1><strong>THIS ROLE IS NOT FOR YOU IF</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Your AI experience is adding a chat window to an existing product. This role is about making intelligence provably correct, which is much harder.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You want requirements handed to you fully specified. Here, you create structure where none exists.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You need consensus before acting. You will make calls with incomplete information and own the outcome.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You are optimizing for a slower pace right now. This is one of the highest-intensity seats in the company, and one that will help define the future of Allocate.</p></li></ul><h1><strong>DETAILS</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Reports to: </strong>Head of Product, working directly with the CEO on data and intelligence strategy.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location: </strong>Palo Alto, CA.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Compensation: </strong>Base salary of $190K to $230K plus discretionary bonus, and equity.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Benefits: </strong>Medical, dental, vision, responsible time off (RTO), 401(k). Allocate is an equal opportunity employer. We value diversity of thought, background, and experience.</p><h1><strong>WHY THIS IS WORTH YOUR TIME</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Most AI product roles are a feature bolted onto someone else’s product. This one is the product. You will own the layer that decides whether clients trust and understand their portfolios, from the extraction intelligence that makes the data reliable to the analysis that makes it meaningful, and you will be measured on whether it is probably right. If you want to build AI that real people stake real decisions on, this is the seat.</p>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT ALLOCATE\n\nAllocate is building the intelligent private markets operating system for the wealth channel. We give RIAs, family offices, and institutional allocators modern infrastructure for discovering, accessing, and managing private market investments. Today that means 350+ wealth advisory firms, 1,500+ GP relationships, and over $5 billion in platform assets, and we are scaling fast.\n\n\nABOUT THE ROLE\n\nYou will own the intelligence layer of Allocate: the AI systems that turn raw private markets documents and data into insight clients trust and act on.\n\nThe raw material is some of the messiest data in finance: capital account statements, fund documents, cash flow notices, unstructured PDFs in a thousand formats. Underneath your product sits a data and extraction pipeline, built in close partnership with our Data Operations team, that turns those inputs into a structured, reliable data layer. You own that pipeline as a product, and your mandate is to make it AI-native end to end: extraction, structuring, validation, and quality handled by intelligence, not brute-force human effort.\n\nBut the pipeline is the substrate, not the product. The product is what the intelligence does with it: surfacing patterns in investment performance and outcomes that no advisor would find by reading raw numbers, powering our Insights and Diligence products, and answering the question every end investor actually has, which is \"how is my portfolio really doing, and what should I pay attention to?\" You will decide where models create real leverage, design the systems that keep their output accurate enough to put in front of paying clients, and ship intelligence that is measurably right, not just impressive in a demo.\n\nThat last part is the hard part, and it is why this role exists. Anyone can wire an LLM to a database. Making AI-generated analysis reliable enough that an RIA will present it to their client requires evals, monitoring, quality gates, and product judgment about when the system is good enough to ship and when it is not. We hold AI features to hard eval gates before they reach clients. You will own those gates.\n\nThis is deliberately a wide seat: the pipeline, the client-facing data experience, and the intelligence on top. We keep them together because splitting them produces exactly the disconnected, half-trusted data products this industry is full of. If that scope reads as too much, this is not your role. If it reads as the whole point, keep going.\n\n\nWHY THIS ROLE MATTERS\n\nIn private markets, data is the product. When an advisor opens a client’s portfolio, the completeness of the look-through data, the accuracy of the cash flows, and the quality of the analytics are the product experience. When the end investor asks how their portfolio is really doing, the answer is only as good as the intelligence built on top of the data.\n\nThis role decides whether that answer is trustworthy and illuminating or incomplete and flat. Your impact shows up in how much manual extraction work intelligence eliminates, how confidently an RIA puts our numbers and our AI-generated analysis in front of their clients, and how often the system surfaces something about performance or outcomes the user would never have found on their own.\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL OWN\n\n - The AI intelligence layer. The models, agents, and systems that generate insights about investment performance and outcomes across Insights, Diligence, and other data-driven products. You decide what gets built, where AI creates leverage versus noise, and what ships.\n\n - Evals and quality gates. AI output that reaches clients passes hard, automated evaluation first. You define what \"correct\" means for each feature, build the eval and monitoring systems that enforce it, and hold the line when something is not ready. Stale, wrong, or hallucinated output in front of a client is a product failure you own.\n\n - The AI-native data pipeline. In close partnership with Data Operations, the extraction and structuring services that turn raw documents into reliable inputs, with intelligence progressively replacing manual work. Their firsthand knowledge of what breaks is your best product input.\n\n - The client-facing data experience. How advisors, operations teams, investment teams, and end investors access and understand portfolio data: look-through investments, cash flows, performance, and cash flow modeling. Sophisticated data made clear and intuitive, down to the column order, the tooltip, and every word of copy.\n\n - Data quality as a product. Completeness, accuracy, and reliability are measured, improved, and held to a standard. These numbers go in front of clients; there is no tolerance for incorrect data, period.\n\n\nHOW YOU’LL BE MEASURED\n\nThis seat comes with a scoreboard, and you will want one.\n\n - Within 90 days, you own the quality metrics we stand behind with clients: eval pass rates on AI-generated output, data completeness and accuracy, and monitoring that catches problems before clients do.\n\n - Within six months, you have shipped a measurable step-change in either extraction leverage (intelligence replacing manual work per document) or client-facing insight (AI-generated analysis clients act on), with the eval evidence to prove it works.\n\n - Ongoing, you present outcomes directly to the CEO. Not status updates. Outcomes: what shipped, what moved, what you’re killing and why.\n\n\nWHO YOU ARE\n\n - You have shipped real AI products, not just used AI tools. You have taken LLM-powered or model-driven features from prototype to production, lived the gap between a great demo and a reliable product, and built or owned the evals that closed it. You have opinions about hallucination rates, grounding, and when an agentic approach beats a deterministic one, because you have paid for the wrong answer before.\n\n - You’ve lived this industry. 7+ years in product in fintech, ideally across investment data products in wealth management, asset management, or private markets. You know what RIAs, fund managers, and their investors expect: the data, the conventions, the standards.\n\n - You operate with extreme ownership. If the data is wrong, you fix it at the source. If the model output is wrong, you find out before the client does. Nobody has to ask, and nothing is someone else’s job.\n\n - You are obsessive about correctness. A single wrong cash flow, misstated return, or confidently wrong AI insight breaks trust with an advisor. You build the systems and standards that prevent it, and you will not rest until the experience is right, down to the last tooltip and word of copy.\n\n - You live on client calls and treat Data Operations and client-facing teams like partners, not a ticket queue. You find the real problem and build the thing that actually solves it, rigorous enough for an investment team and intuitive enough for an end investor. You prototype with modern AI tools daily and raise that standard for everyone around you.\n\n\nTHIS ROLE IS NOT FOR YOU IF\n\n - Your AI experience is adding a chat window to an existing product. This role is about making intelligence provably correct, which is much harder.\n\n - You want requirements handed to you fully specified. Here, you create structure where none exists.\n\n - You need consensus before acting. You will make calls with incomplete information and own the outcome.\n\n - You are optimizing for a slower pace right now. This is one of the highest-intensity seats in the company, and one that will help define the future of Allocate.\n\n\nDETAILS\n\nReports to: Head of Product, working directly with the CEO on data and intelligence strategy.\n\nLocation: Palo Alto, CA.\n\nCompensation: Base salary of $190K to $230K plus discretionary bonus, and equity.\n\nBenefits: Medical, dental, vision, responsible time off (RTO), 401(k). Allocate is an equal opportunity employer. We value diversity of thought, background, and experience.\n\n\nWHY THIS IS WORTH YOUR TIME\n\nMost AI product roles are a feature bolted onto someone else’s product. This one is the product. You will own the layer that decides whether clients trust and understand their portfolios, from the extraction intelligence that makes the data reliable to the analysis that makes it meaningful, and you will be measured on whether it is probably right. If you want to build AI that real people stake real decisions on, this is the seat.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$190K – $230K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$190K - $230K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"7549fc38-3027-4036-8dbf-f7e3f439b387","tierSummary":"$190K – $230K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"58abacc7-66d2-4984-8540-bbe927cf86ff","summary":"$190K – $230K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":190000,"maxValue":230000},{"id":"b339cebb-3aad-43b4-b406-6cd499231f2b","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":190000,"maxValue":230000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"a1cdc39f-2fde-4a83-a8a4-fe01add21410","title":"Sr. Data Engineer II","department":"Software Engineering","team":"Software Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Palo Alto Office (Hybrid)","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-08T21:20:23.606+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Palo Alto"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/allocate/a1cdc39f-2fde-4a83-a8a4-fe01add21410","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/allocate/a1cdc39f-2fde-4a83-a8a4-fe01add21410/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Allocate</strong> </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Allocate is transforming private market investing by enabling RIAs and family offices to seamlessly discover, model, and manage their private market exposure. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our platform combines curated fund and co-investment opportunities with institutional-grade infrastructure. Through a single, data-rich digital experience, clients access top-tier opportunities across venture capital, private equity, private credit, and other private asset classes—backed by powerful tracking, analytics, and administration tools. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Job Description </strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Allocate is looking for a Senior Data Engineer to help build out the data infrastructure that powers our analytics, reporting, and data-driven product features. As a fintech startup on a mission to make investing in top-tier private markets more accessible, we have a wealth of financial and investment data to harness. Our data lead has established the foundational architecture and strategy, and we are now looking for a strong senior engineer to help extend, scale, and harden it. In this role you will partner closely with our data lead to model core financial entities, integrate internal and external sources, and build the pipelines and infrastructure that let our engineering and product teams make informed decisions and ship compelling features. This is a hybrid position based out of our Palo Alto, CA office, where you will work alongside our backend team (C#/.NET) and frontend team (Node/Vue.js) to integrate data pipelines into our platform. If you are a hands-on engineer who wants to do high-impact data work in a collaborative startup environment, we want to hear from you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Responsibilities</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build and Extend Data Architecture: </strong>Build on and extend Allocate's data lakehouse on AWS, combining data lake storage and warehouse technologies to store diverse financial datasets. Contribute to our knowledge graph that models key relationships (investors, funds, companies, etc.) and to the vector database integration that stores embeddings for semantic search and retrieval across our AI agents, models, and providers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Develop Data Pipelines: </strong>Create robust ETL/ELT pipelines to ingest, clean, and transform data from various sources (internal application data and third-party APIs). Ensure both batch processing and real-time data streaming are handled to support up-to-date analytics and recommendations. Build pipelines with an eye on scalability (able to handle increasing data volume and complexity) and reliability (proper error handling and monitoring).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Enable AI/ML Capabilities: </strong>Work closely with our data science and engineering team to provision the data and infrastructure needed for machine learning models and AI features. This includes preparing training datasets, setting up feature stores, and orchestrating workflows that feed LLM-based agents with the context they need (e.g. retrieving relevant data via vector similarity search). You will also help implement systems to serve AI model outputs (such as recommendations) back into the product in real time.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Engineering Excellence and Collaboration: </strong>Partner with our data lead and the broader engineering team to deliver data and AI infrastructure. Raise the bar through thoughtful code review, testing, and adherence to best practices, and help engineers who consume data in their services do so effectively. Work in cross-functional squads to incorporate data-driven features into the product roadmap, and share your expertise with peers as the team grows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Infrastructure and DevOps: </strong>Collaborate with our DevOps engineers to deploy and maintain data services. Containerize and orchestrate data tools (using Docker/Kubernetes on AWS EKS) for production use. Implement CI/CD pipelines for data workflows so that changes to data processing or models are tested and deployed automatically. Monitor the health and performance of our data platforms (setting up alerts, dashboards) and be ready to troubleshoot and resolve issues in production to ensure uptime of critical data and AI services.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Continuous Improvement: </strong>Stay up to date with the latest in data engineering and AI, from new AWS offerings to open-source ML tools. Evaluate and recommend new technologies, for example assessing whether a stream processing platform like Kafka/Kinesis or an orchestration tool like Airflow could improve pipeline reliability. Challenge conventions and innovate: we encourage rethinking how things are done as we push to build a world-class, intelligent platform.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What You'll Need to Succeed</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Strong Data Engineering Experience: </strong>5+ years of hands-on experience in data engineering (or related fields), including designing and building large-scale data pipelines and storage solutions. You should have taken projects through the full lifecycle from design to production deployment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Cloud Proficiency (AWS): </strong>Strong experience working with AWS cloud services for data. You should be comfortable with tools like S3, EC2, ECS, EKS, Athena, Redshift, Glue, and Step Functions. Experience setting up infrastructure-as-code (Terraform/CloudFormation) for these services is a plus.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Database and Data Modeling Skills: </strong>Proficiency in SQL and relational database design. Able to design efficient schemas and optimize queries/indexes for performance. Experience building or working with data warehouses or lakehouses (e.g. Snowflake, Databricks Delta Lake) is highly desired. Familiarity with graph databases (Neo4j, AWS Neptune, etc.) and knowledge graph schemas will help you hit the ground running.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Programming Expertise: </strong>Fluency in at least one major programming language used in data engineering. Python is commonly used for data pipelines, and pandas/PySpark experience is valuable. We also value experience with TypeScript/Node.js in data contexts, since our stack leans toward modern web technologies. The ideal candidate can work across languages, for example writing a data API in C# or Node.js to interface with our backend while also crafting Python scripts for data processing. Clean, maintainable code and adherence to best practices are a must.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>AI/ML Familiarity: </strong>While this is not a pure ML researcher role, you should understand how machine learning models consume data. Experience preparing datasets for training, working with feature stores, or integrating ML model outputs into applications is important. Knowledge of vector embeddings and experience with vector databases (Postgres pgvector, Chroma, Pinecone, etc.) is a big plus, as our AI features rely on semantic search. Familiarity with frameworks for building AI agents or retrieval-augmented generation (e.g. LangChain, LlamaIndex) is also valuable.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>AI-Native Mindset: </strong>treating AI as core to the workflow, fluency with agentic tools and LLM-assisted dev, pushing the frontier of AI tooling.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>DevOps and DataOps Skills: </strong>Solid understanding of containerization and deployment. Experience using Docker to package data applications and Kubernetes (or AWS EKS) to run distributed jobs/services. You should be comfortable setting up CI/CD pipelines for automated testing and deployment of data pipelines or ML models. Experience with workflow managers (Airflow, Prefect, dbt, or similar) is beneficial.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Strong Analytical and Problem-Solving Skills: </strong>Ability to analyze complex data problems, debug pipeline issues, and optimize system performance. You should be detail-oriented about data correctness and have a knack for troubleshooting data discrepancies or bottlenecks in processing.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Compliance and Security: </strong>working in a regulated SEC environment, handling sensitive investor/financial data, building with auditability, least-privilege, and data governance in mind. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Collaboration and Communication: </strong>Excellent communication skills and a collaborative mindset. You will be working with a diverse fully-remote team, so you need to articulate ideas clearly and build consensus. Comfort mentoring peers and driving technical projects to completion is important, as is a positive attitude toward continuous learning and improvement. We value growth mindset and adaptability.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Education:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, similar technical field of study, or equivalent practical experience</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Essential Values &amp; Culture:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Providing our clients with a world-class experience is our number one priority. We obsessively search for ways to improve the experience for our clients and partners. This requires extraordinary response times, proactivity, and ensuring that everything we do, from product strategy to offline communications is a top-tier client experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Challenge convention: </strong>Instead of detailing all the reasons why an idea may not work, we constantly question things to determine how a viable idea may be put into motion.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Commitment to continuous improvement: </strong>We find ways to personally scale each day by pushing ourselves up the learning curve.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Meritocracy, not politics: </strong>We place the utmost value on results and rewards through merit, not reward actions driven by political agendas or behavior.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Civil Discourse is embraced: </strong>We believe open, intellectually curious conversations are required to consistently arrive at the best decisions. Respect is paramount in our dealings with one another, but our mission is always to get the right answer collectively, not to be right.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Embrace technological change: </strong>We adopt tools and techniques that make us faster, smarter, and better. We stay open to innovation, especially around AI and automation, and drop outdated methods without hesitation. Complacency kills progress, we value adaptability and curiosity.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Additional Details:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location: </strong>Palo Alto (hybrid)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Employment:</strong> Full-time</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Seniority: </strong>Mid-level professional</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Salary: </strong>Total compensation may also include a discretionary performance-based bonus. The expected base salary range for this role is $145,000 to $220,000. </p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">      <em>Actual compensation will be determined based on the candidate's primary work location             and other job-related factors including skills, experience, qualifications, interview                            performance, internal equity, and market data. Candidates located in higher cost-of-living           markets, including the San Francisco Bay Area, may be considered within the higher end of the range.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>      This range reflects base salary only and does not include bonus, equity, benefits or other              forms of compensation that may be offered.  Total compensation may also include a                      discretionary performance-based bonus.</em></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Benefits:</strong> Medical, dental, and vision. 401(k), and responsible vacation time (PTO)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Travel required for team/department offsites</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">An in-person interview may be required during the interview process</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A Broadband internet connection required</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Compliance with Allocate's Code of Ethics is a given for this role.</p></li></ul>","descriptionPlain":"About Allocate \n\nAllocate is transforming private market investing by enabling RIAs and family offices to seamlessly discover, model, and manage their private market exposure. \n\nOur platform combines curated fund and co-investment opportunities with institutional-grade infrastructure. Through a single, data-rich digital experience, clients access top-tier opportunities across venture capital, private equity, private credit, and other private asset classes—backed by powerful tracking, analytics, and administration tools. \n\n\n\nJob Description \n\nAllocate is looking for a Senior Data Engineer to help build out the data infrastructure that powers our analytics, reporting, and data-driven product features. As a fintech startup on a mission to make investing in top-tier private markets more accessible, we have a wealth of financial and investment data to harness. Our data lead has established the foundational architecture and strategy, and we are now looking for a strong senior engineer to help extend, scale, and harden it. In this role you will partner closely with our data lead to model core financial entities, integrate internal and external sources, and build the pipelines and infrastructure that let our engineering and product teams make informed decisions and ship compelling features. This is a hybrid position based out of our Palo Alto, CA office, where you will work alongside our backend team (C#/.NET) and frontend team (Node/Vue.js) to integrate data pipelines into our platform. If you are a hands-on engineer who wants to do high-impact data work in a collaborative startup environment, we want to hear from you.\n\n\n\nResponsibilities\n\n - Build and Extend Data Architecture: Build on and extend Allocate's data lakehouse on AWS, combining data lake storage and warehouse technologies to store diverse financial datasets. Contribute to our knowledge graph that models key relationships (investors, funds, companies, etc.) and to the vector database integration that stores embeddings for semantic search and retrieval across our AI agents, models, and providers.\n\n - Develop Data Pipelines: Create robust ETL/ELT pipelines to ingest, clean, and transform data from various sources (internal application data and third-party APIs). Ensure both batch processing and real-time data streaming are handled to support up-to-date analytics and recommendations. Build pipelines with an eye on scalability (able to handle increasing data volume and complexity) and reliability (proper error handling and monitoring).\n\n - Enable AI/ML Capabilities: Work closely with our data science and engineering team to provision the data and infrastructure needed for machine learning models and AI features. This includes preparing training datasets, setting up feature stores, and orchestrating workflows that feed LLM-based agents with the context they need (e.g. retrieving relevant data via vector similarity search). You will also help implement systems to serve AI model outputs (such as recommendations) back into the product in real time.\n\n - Engineering Excellence and Collaboration: Partner with our data lead and the broader engineering team to deliver data and AI infrastructure. Raise the bar through thoughtful code review, testing, and adherence to best practices, and help engineers who consume data in their services do so effectively. Work in cross-functional squads to incorporate data-driven features into the product roadmap, and share your expertise with peers as the team grows.\n\n - Infrastructure and DevOps: Collaborate with our DevOps engineers to deploy and maintain data services. Containerize and orchestrate data tools (using Docker/Kubernetes on AWS EKS) for production use. Implement CI/CD pipelines for data workflows so that changes to data processing or models are tested and deployed automatically. Monitor the health and performance of our data platforms (setting up alerts, dashboards) and be ready to troubleshoot and resolve issues in production to ensure uptime of critical data and AI services.\n\n - Continuous Improvement: Stay up to date with the latest in data engineering and AI, from new AWS offerings to open-source ML tools. Evaluate and recommend new technologies, for example assessing whether a stream processing platform like Kafka/Kinesis or an orchestration tool like Airflow could improve pipeline reliability. Challenge conventions and innovate: we encourage rethinking how things are done as we push to build a world-class, intelligent platform.\n\n\n\nWhat You'll Need to Succeed\n\n - Strong Data Engineering Experience: 5+ years of hands-on experience in data engineering (or related fields), including designing and building large-scale data pipelines and storage solutions. You should have taken projects through the full lifecycle from design to production deployment.\n\n - Cloud Proficiency (AWS): Strong experience working with AWS cloud services for data. You should be comfortable with tools like S3, EC2, ECS, EKS, Athena, Redshift, Glue, and Step Functions. Experience setting up infrastructure-as-code (Terraform/CloudFormation) for these services is a plus.\n\n - Database and Data Modeling Skills: Proficiency in SQL and relational database design. Able to design efficient schemas and optimize queries/indexes for performance. Experience building or working with data warehouses or lakehouses (e.g. Snowflake, Databricks Delta Lake) is highly desired. Familiarity with graph databases (Neo4j, AWS Neptune, etc.) and knowledge graph schemas will help you hit the ground running.\n\n - Programming Expertise: Fluency in at least one major programming language used in data engineering. Python is commonly used for data pipelines, and pandas/PySpark experience is valuable. We also value experience with TypeScript/Node.js in data contexts, since our stack leans toward modern web technologies. The ideal candidate can work across languages, for example writing a data API in C# or Node.js to interface with our backend while also crafting Python scripts for data processing. Clean, maintainable code and adherence to best practices are a must.\n\n - AI/ML Familiarity: While this is not a pure ML researcher role, you should understand how machine learning models consume data. Experience preparing datasets for training, working with feature stores, or integrating ML model outputs into applications is important. Knowledge of vector embeddings and experience with vector databases (Postgres pgvector, Chroma, Pinecone, etc.) is a big plus, as our AI features rely on semantic search. Familiarity with frameworks for building AI agents or retrieval-augmented generation (e.g. LangChain, LlamaIndex) is also valuable.\n\n - AI-Native Mindset: treating AI as core to the workflow, fluency with agentic tools and LLM-assisted dev, pushing the frontier of AI tooling.\n\n - DevOps and DataOps Skills: Solid understanding of containerization and deployment. Experience using Docker to package data applications and Kubernetes (or AWS EKS) to run distributed jobs/services. You should be comfortable setting up CI/CD pipelines for automated testing and deployment of data pipelines or ML models. Experience with workflow managers (Airflow, Prefect, dbt, or similar) is beneficial.\n\n - Strong Analytical and Problem-Solving Skills: Ability to analyze complex data problems, debug pipeline issues, and optimize system performance. You should be detail-oriented about data correctness and have a knack for troubleshooting data discrepancies or bottlenecks in processing.\n\n - Compliance and Security: working in a regulated SEC environment, handling sensitive investor/financial data, building with auditability, least-privilege, and data governance in mind. \n\n - Collaboration and Communication: Excellent communication skills and a collaborative mindset. You will be working with a diverse fully-remote team, so you need to articulate ideas clearly and build consensus. Comfort mentoring peers and driving technical projects to completion is important, as is a positive attitude toward continuous learning and improvement. We value growth mindset and adaptability.\n\nEducation:\n\nBachelor’s degree in Computer Science, similar technical field of study, or equivalent practical experience\n\nEssential Values & Culture:\n\n - Providing our clients with a world-class experience is our number one priority. We obsessively search for ways to improve the experience for our clients and partners. This requires extraordinary response times, proactivity, and ensuring that everything we do, from product strategy to offline communications is a top-tier client experience.\n\n - Challenge convention: Instead of detailing all the reasons why an idea may not work, we constantly question things to determine how a viable idea may be put into motion.\n\n - Commitment to continuous improvement: We find ways to personally scale each day by pushing ourselves up the learning curve.\n\n - Meritocracy, not politics: We place the utmost value on results and rewards through merit, not reward actions driven by political agendas or behavior.\n\n - Civil Discourse is embraced: We believe open, intellectually curious conversations are required to consistently arrive at the best decisions. Respect is paramount in our dealings with one another, but our mission is always to get the right answer collectively, not to be right.\n\n - Embrace technological change: We adopt tools and techniques that make us faster, smarter, and better. We stay open to innovation, especially around AI and automation, and drop outdated methods without hesitation. Complacency kills progress, we value adaptability and curiosity.\n\nAdditional Details:\n\n - Location: Palo Alto (hybrid)\n\n - Employment: Full-time\n\n - Seniority: Mid-level professional\n\n - Salary: Total compensation may also include a discretionary performance-based bonus. The expected base salary range for this role is $145,000 to $220,000. \n\n      Actual compensation will be determined based on the candidate's primary work location             and other job-related factors including skills, experience, qualifications, interview                            performance, internal equity, and market data. Candidates located in higher cost-of-living           markets, including the San Francisco Bay Area, may be considered within the higher end of the range.\n\n      This range reflects base salary only and does not include bonus, equity, benefits or other              forms of compensation that may be offered.  Total compensation may also include a                      discretionary performance-based bonus.\n\n - Benefits: Medical, dental, and vision. 401(k), and responsible vacation time (PTO)\n\n - Travel required for team/department offsites\n\n - An in-person interview may be required during the interview process\n\n - A Broadband internet connection required\n\n - Compliance with Allocate's Code of Ethics is a given for this role.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$145K – $220K","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$145K - $220K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"b0150b94-4963-4650-a928-5c9ab7509e8f","tierSummary":"$145K – $220K","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"358d8450-622e-499a-8884-b810b02d712a","summary":"$145K – $220K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":145000,"maxValue":220000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":145000,"maxValue":220000}]}},{"id":"181ec502-9605-424f-8e93-56bfe8255b3a","title":"Information Technology (IT) Specialist","department":"Operations","team":"Operations","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Palo Alto Office (Hybrid)","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-08T21:30:00.758+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Palo Alto"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/allocate/181ec502-9605-424f-8e93-56bfe8255b3a","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/allocate/181ec502-9605-424f-8e93-56bfe8255b3a/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Allocate is transforming private market investing by enabling RIAs and family offices to seamlessly discover, model, and manage their private market exposure. Our platform combines curated fund and co-investment opportunities with institutional-grade infrastructure, serving clients across venture capital, private equity, private credit, and other private asset classes — backed by powerful tracking, analytics, and administration tools.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are seeking a dedicated IT Specialist to join our growing team. In this role, you will manage system upgrades, resolve user queries, and optimize our technology infrastructure to align with business goals. As an integral part of our operations, you will drive efficiency and innovation while safeguarding our digital assets. If you are passionate about technology and thrive on IT driven innovation, we encourage you to apply. We offer a collaborative work culture, meaningful opportunities for professional development, and a competitive benefits package.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>About the Role</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a generalist IT role with meaningful depth expectations across three core areas: day-to-day troubleshooting and end-user support; systems and infrastructure management spanning SaaS, IdP, and MDM; and security-adjacent operations supporting our SOC 2 compliance posture. You will serve as the primary internal IT point of contact for an in-office and remote workforce of 80+ employees, while also coordinating execution with our managed service partner (MSP) on infrastructure and support tasks.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Security is not a separate workstream in this role, it is the operating standard applied to every IT task, from provisioning to asset management to vendor coordination. The right candidate moves fluidly between tactical support tickets and strategic systems work, brings a security-aware mindset to everything they do, and is energized by operating in a fast-moving, high-growth fintech environment.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Essential Responsibilities and Duties</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>End-User Support</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide Tier 1/2 support across hardware, software, and SaaS applications for in-office and remote workforce</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assist MSP with new user device, account, and software/application provisioning</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Respond to technical support tickets from employees facing technical difficulties</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Troubleshoot connectivity, access, and productivity tool issues (Google Workspace, Slack, and core SaaS tools)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conduct guidance sessions on IT tools, security practices, and system usage</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain internal IT documentation, runbooks, and knowledge base articles</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Systems &amp; Infrastructure</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support onboarding, offboarding and management of user accounts, permissions, and access controls across IT systems and the company's SaaS footprint</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support provisioning and deprovisioning across the company's SaaS application footprint</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Install, update, and maintain software applications, ensuring compatibility and data security</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Perform routine resource optimization to maximize license and reduce operational costs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate with vendors for device purchases, warranties, and external support services</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain and improve IT asset inventory and hardware tracking processes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate with the MSP partner on escalations, infrastructure tasks, and project execution</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Security Operations &amp; Compliance</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support the Information Security program by assisting in access reviews documentation, MFA enforcement, and endpoint compliance checks</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assist in maintaining evidence for SOC 2 Type II compliance (Security, Availability, and Confidentiality trust service criteria)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Analyze data from logs to improve performance and proactively identify risks</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monitor and respond to alerts from endpoint management and security tooling</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in security initiatives, as needed under the direction of the Information Security</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help enforce IT and security policies and contribute to policy documentation as needed</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Required Skills and Qualifications</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bachelor’s degree in information technology, Computer Science, or a related field, or equivalent practical experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3–5 years of demonstrable experience as an IT Specialist, IT Administrator, or in a technical support, system analysis, or network administration role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficiency in operating systems: macOS, iOS, Windows and common network technologies</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience administering Google Workspace (user management, Groups, directory, OAuth app controls and environmental hardening)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with SaaS access management and SSO concepts (SAML, SCIM, OAuth)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Knowledge of network administration protocols, firewalls, and IT security best practices</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understanding of cybersecurity principles and data protection practices</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with IT help desk systems and ticketing tools</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong troubleshooting and problem-solving skills across hardware, software, and cloud applications</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent interpersonal and communication skills to interact with both technical and non-technical stakeholders</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to work independently and manage multiple priorities in a fast-moving environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Attention to detail and organizational skills to handle concurrent tasks efficiently</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Preferred Skills and Qualifications</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Relevant professional certifications: CompTIA A+, Network+, Security+, Google IT Support Professional</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience supporting or contributing to a SOC 2 audit or compliance program</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with cybersecurity frameworks such as NIST or ISO 27001</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with cloud computing platforms (AWS, Microsoft Azure, or Google Cloud)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Knowledge of ITIL frameworks for IT service management</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with remote monitoring and management (RMM) tools</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience coordinating with a managed service provider (MSP) in a hybrid support model</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exposure to fintech, financial services, or other regulated industries</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Essential Values &amp; Culture</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Providing our clients with a world-class experience is our number one priority. We obsessively search for ways to improve the experience for our clients and partners. This requires extraordinary response times, proactivity, and ensuring that everything we do — from product strategy to offline communications — reflects a top-tier client experience.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Challenge convention:</strong> Instead of detailing all the reasons why an idea may not work, we constantly question things to determine how a viable idea may be put into motion.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Commitment to continuous improvement:</strong> We find ways to personally scale each day by pushing ourselves up the learning curve.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Meritocracy, not politics:</strong> We place the utmost value on results and rewards through merit, not reward actions driven by political agendas or behavior.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Civil Discourse is embraced:</strong> We believe open, intellectually curious conversations are required to consistently arrive at the best decisions. Respect is paramount in our dealings with one another, but our mission is always to get the right answer collectively, not to be right.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Embrace technological change:</strong> We adopt tools and techniques that make us faster, smarter, and better. We stay open to innovation, especially around AI and automation, and drop outdated methods without hesitation. This includes actively integrating AI-assisted tools into your daily workflow and staying current as the landscape evolves. Complacency kills progress — we value adaptability and curiosity.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Additional Details</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fully Hybrid Position</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Travel may be required for company offsites</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Broadband internet connection required</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Location: All I-9 eligible candidates will be considered</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Salary: $100K–$125K base, with bonus and equity eligibility</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Benefits: Medical, dental, and vision; 401(k); and responsible vacation time (PTO)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Employment: Full-time</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The base pay offered will be determined based on the candidate's experience, location, skills, training, certifications, education, internal equity, and market data. Total compensation may also include a discretionary performance-based bonus. We do not anticipate that candidates hired will begin at the top of the range, though this may occur on a case-by-case basis.</p>","descriptionPlain":"OVERVIEW\n\nAllocate is transforming private market investing by enabling RIAs and family offices to seamlessly discover, model, and manage their private market exposure. Our platform combines curated fund and co-investment opportunities with institutional-grade infrastructure, serving clients across venture capital, private equity, private credit, and other private asset classes — backed by powerful tracking, analytics, and administration tools.\n\nWe are seeking a dedicated IT Specialist to join our growing team. In this role, you will manage system upgrades, resolve user queries, and optimize our technology infrastructure to align with business goals. As an integral part of our operations, you will drive efficiency and innovation while safeguarding our digital assets. If you are passionate about technology and thrive on IT driven innovation, we encourage you to apply. We offer a collaborative work culture, meaningful opportunities for professional development, and a competitive benefits package.\n\n\n\n\nABOUT THE ROLE\n\nThis is a generalist IT role with meaningful depth expectations across three core areas: day-to-day troubleshooting and end-user support; systems and infrastructure management spanning SaaS, IdP, and MDM; and security-adjacent operations supporting our SOC 2 compliance posture. You will serve as the primary internal IT point of contact for an in-office and remote workforce of 80+ employees, while also coordinating execution with our managed service partner (MSP) on infrastructure and support tasks.\n\nSecurity is not a separate workstream in this role, it is the operating standard applied to every IT task, from provisioning to asset management to vendor coordination. The right candidate moves fluidly between tactical support tickets and strategic systems work, brings a security-aware mindset to everything they do, and is energized by operating in a fast-moving, high-growth fintech environment.\n\n\n\n\nESSENTIAL RESPONSIBILITIES AND DUTIES\n\nEnd-User Support\n\n - Provide Tier 1/2 support across hardware, software, and SaaS applications for in-office and remote workforce\n\n - Assist MSP with new user device, account, and software/application provisioning\n\n - Respond to technical support tickets from employees facing technical difficulties\n\n - Troubleshoot connectivity, access, and productivity tool issues (Google Workspace, Slack, and core SaaS tools)\n\n - Conduct guidance sessions on IT tools, security practices, and system usage\n\n - Maintain internal IT documentation, runbooks, and knowledge base articles\n\n\n\nSystems & Infrastructure\n\n - Support onboarding, offboarding and management of user accounts, permissions, and access controls across IT systems and the company's SaaS footprint\n\n - Support provisioning and deprovisioning across the company's SaaS application footprint\n\n - Install, update, and maintain software applications, ensuring compatibility and data security\n\n - Perform routine resource optimization to maximize license and reduce operational costs\n\n - Coordinate with vendors for device purchases, warranties, and external support services\n\n - Maintain and improve IT asset inventory and hardware tracking processes\n\n - Coordinate with the MSP partner on escalations, infrastructure tasks, and project execution\n\n\n\nSecurity Operations & Compliance\n\n - Support the Information Security program by assisting in access reviews documentation, MFA enforcement, and endpoint compliance checks\n\n - Assist in maintaining evidence for SOC 2 Type II compliance (Security, Availability, and Confidentiality trust service criteria)\n\n - Analyze data from logs to improve performance and proactively identify risks\n\n - Monitor and respond to alerts from endpoint management and security tooling\n\n - Participate in security initiatives, as needed under the direction of the Information Security\n\n - Help enforce IT and security policies and contribute to policy documentation as needed\n\n\n\n\nREQUIRED SKILLS AND QUALIFICATIONS\n\n - Bachelor’s degree in information technology, Computer Science, or a related field, or equivalent practical experience\n\n - 3–5 years of demonstrable experience as an IT Specialist, IT Administrator, or in a technical support, system analysis, or network administration role\n\n - Proficiency in operating systems: macOS, iOS, Windows and common network technologies\n\n - Hands-on experience administering Google Workspace (user management, Groups, directory, OAuth app controls and environmental hardening)\n\n - Familiarity with SaaS access management and SSO concepts (SAML, SCIM, OAuth)\n\n - Knowledge of network administration protocols, firewalls, and IT security best practices\n\n - Understanding of cybersecurity principles and data protection practices\n\n - Familiarity with IT help desk systems and ticketing tools\n\n - Strong troubleshooting and problem-solving skills across hardware, software, and cloud applications\n\n - Excellent interpersonal and communication skills to interact with both technical and non-technical stakeholders\n\n - Ability to work independently and manage multiple priorities in a fast-moving environment\n\n - Attention to detail and organizational skills to handle concurrent tasks efficiently\n\n\n\n\nPREFERRED SKILLS AND QUALIFICATIONS\n\n - Relevant professional certifications: CompTIA A+, Network+, Security+, Google IT Support Professional\n\n - Experience supporting or contributing to a SOC 2 audit or compliance program\n\n - Familiarity with cybersecurity frameworks such as NIST or ISO 27001\n\n - Familiarity with cloud computing platforms (AWS, Microsoft Azure, or Google Cloud)\n\n - Knowledge of ITIL frameworks for IT service management\n\n - Experience with remote monitoring and management (RMM) tools\n\n - Experience coordinating with a managed service provider (MSP) in a hybrid support model\n\n - Exposure to fintech, financial services, or other regulated industries\n\n\n\n\nESSENTIAL VALUES & CULTURE\n\nProviding our clients with a world-class experience is our number one priority. We obsessively search for ways to improve the experience for our clients and partners. This requires extraordinary response times, proactivity, and ensuring that everything we do — from product strategy to offline communications — reflects a top-tier client experience.\n\n\n\n - Challenge convention: Instead of detailing all the reasons why an idea may not work, we constantly question things to determine how a viable idea may be put into motion.\n\n - Commitment to continuous improvement: We find ways to personally scale each day by pushing ourselves up the learning curve.\n\n - Meritocracy, not politics: We place the utmost value on results and rewards through merit, not reward actions driven by political agendas or behavior.\n\n - Civil Discourse is embraced: We believe open, intellectually curious conversations are required to consistently arrive at the best decisions. Respect is paramount in our dealings with one another, but our mission is always to get the right answer collectively, not to be right.\n\n - Embrace technological change: We adopt tools and techniques that make us faster, smarter, and better. We stay open to innovation, especially around AI and automation, and drop outdated methods without hesitation. This includes actively integrating AI-assisted tools into your daily workflow and staying current as the landscape evolves. Complacency kills progress — we value adaptability and curiosity.\n\n\n\n\nADDITIONAL DETAILS\n\n - Fully Hybrid Position\n\n - Travel may be required for company offsites\n\n - Broadband internet connection required\n\n - Location: All I-9 eligible candidates will be considered\n\n - Salary: $100K–$125K base, with bonus and equity eligibility\n\n - Benefits: Medical, dental, and vision; 401(k); and responsible vacation time (PTO)\n\n - Employment: Full-time\n\n\n\nThe base pay offered will be determined based on the candidate's experience, location, skills, training, certifications, education, internal equity, and market data. Total compensation may also include a discretionary performance-based bonus. We do not anticipate that candidates hired will begin at the top of the range, though this may occur on a case-by-case basis.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$100K – $125K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$100K - $125K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"ecf2e746-d650-4d5f-b25a-575ee626a198","tierSummary":"$100K – $125K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"0a3e231e-a100-45fd-88bc-fbc9b17c32cd","summary":"$100K – $125K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":100000,"maxValue":125000},{"id":"f0f90e5d-a32d-4fe8-bf5f-6e52815b3d66","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":100000,"maxValue":125000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"0e915511-1e86-4ca5-bc99-841cfc4ebe2d","title":"Fund Formation Attorney","department":"Legal","team":"Legal","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York Office (On-Site)","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"Palo Alto (On-Site)","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Palo Alto"}}}],"publishedAt":"2026-07-03T15:53:02.453+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":false,"workplaceType":"OnSite","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/allocate/0e915511-1e86-4ca5-bc99-841cfc4ebe2d","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/allocate/0e915511-1e86-4ca5-bc99-841cfc4ebe2d/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>Job Responsibilities</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a member of Allocate’s legal team, you will play a dynamic and vital role in supporting Allocate’s long-term growth. You will be responsible for providing comprehensive assistance with fund formation, onboarding, fund filings, regulatory compliance, as well as corporate governance matters, and other legal activities. You will also be an active participant in the development and success of Allocate’s technology products. The successful candidate should possess a strong understanding of private fund concepts, along with excellent organizational and communication skills.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Responsibilities include (but would not be limited to):</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Advising on a broad range of legal and regulatory matters related to the formation, distribution/marketing, and operation of private funds and separate account products. This includes preparing and negotiating private placement memoranda, partnership agreements, side letters, placement agreements, investment management agreements, and other fund-related documents.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Supporting the company’s investment activities by reviewing, drafting, and managing engagement letters and other investment-related agreements.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Supporting client and relationship teams on investor onboarding and investor inquiries.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monitoring and ensuring compliance with relevant laws, regulations, and industry standards for registered advisers and private investment funds. Assisting with regulatory filings, including Form ADV, Form PF, and Form D, and coordinating responses to regulatory inquiries.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Handling corporate and entity matters, including forming and maintaining fund vehicles, general partner and management entities; supporting corporate governance, entity management, and maintenance of organizational records; and assisting with the company’s own corporate and commercial matters.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drafting, negotiating, and managing various legal documents, including transaction documents, carry program documents, client agreements, vendor contracts, and NDAs, ensuring they are current and compliant.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Building and maintaining strong working relationships with key business partners, including external counsel, clients, and internal teams, to effectively support Allocate’s business initiatives.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Actively contributing to the development of Allocate’s investment and technology products and initiatives.</p></li></ul><h2>Qualifications</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At least 4 years of experience at a major law firm or in-house legal department working on private funds; experience with open-ended and closed-ended funds a plus.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Juris Doctor degree from an accredited law school and at least one active bar membership/license to practice law in any state.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of the asset management industry and private funds, with detailed knowledge of the securities laws and regulations most relevant to private fund advisers—principally the Investment Advisers Act; the Securities Act and Regulation D (including Rule 506(b)/(c) and the accredited-investor and qualified-purchaser standards); and the Investment Company Act exclusions relied on by private funds (Sections 3(c)(1) and 3(c)(7)). Familiarity with blue-sky/Form D filings and the broker-dealer/FINRA framework is a plus.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to interact professionally with clients and team members.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Willingness to be very hands-on and proactive in offering solutions; comfortable with technology.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong organizational skills with the capability to manage multiple tasks and meet deadlines effectively, while maintaining keen attention to detail and accuracy in all work product.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Essential Values &amp; Culture</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"> <strong>Providing our clients with a world-class experience is our number one priority. </strong>We obsessively search for ways to improve the experience for our clients and partners. This requires extraordinary response times, proactivity, and ensuring that everything we do, from product strategy to offline communications, is a top-tier client experience.</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Challenge convention: </strong>Instead of detailing all the reasons why an idea may not work, we constantly question things to determine how a viable idea may be put into motion.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Commitment to continuous improvement: </strong>We find ways to personally scale each day by pushing ourselves up the learning curve.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Meritocracy, not politics: </strong>We place the utmost value on results and rewards through merit, not reward actions driven by political agendas or behavior.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Civil Discourse is embraced: </strong>We believe open, intellectually curious conversations are required to arrive at the best decisions. Respect is paramount in our dealings with one another, but our mission is always to get the right answer collectively, not to be right.</p></li></ul><h2>Additional Details</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Reporting to: </strong>Senior Counsel</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location: </strong>SF Bay Area, NYC, CT, or Boston preferred; all U.S. candidates will be considered. Hybrid for SF Bay Area and NY offices.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Salary Range: </strong>It is expected that the base annual salary range for this position in the locations listed above will be $180,000 - $210,000. Actual salary will be determined based on the candidate’s experience, location, skills, training, certifications and education, and other relevant qualifications specific to the role, as well as internal equity and market data. Total compensation may also include equity and discretionary performance-based bonus based on factors such as individual and team performance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Benefits: </strong>Medical, dental, vision, responsible time off (RTO), 401k</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Employment: </strong>Full-time</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role will be subject to Allocate’s Code of Ethics and related compliance obligations.</p></li></ul>","descriptionPlain":"JOB RESPONSIBILITIES\n\nAs a member of Allocate’s legal team, you will play a dynamic and vital role in supporting Allocate’s long-term growth. You will be responsible for providing comprehensive assistance with fund formation, onboarding, fund filings, regulatory compliance, as well as corporate governance matters, and other legal activities. You will also be an active participant in the development and success of Allocate’s technology products. The successful candidate should possess a strong understanding of private fund concepts, along with excellent organizational and communication skills.\n\n\n\n\nRESPONSIBILITIES INCLUDE (BUT WOULD NOT BE LIMITED TO):\n\n - Advising on a broad range of legal and regulatory matters related to the formation, distribution/marketing, and operation of private funds and separate account products. This includes preparing and negotiating private placement memoranda, partnership agreements, side letters, placement agreements, investment management agreements, and other fund-related documents.\n\n - Supporting the company’s investment activities by reviewing, drafting, and managing engagement letters and other investment-related agreements.\n\n - Supporting client and relationship teams on investor onboarding and investor inquiries.\n\n - Monitoring and ensuring compliance with relevant laws, regulations, and industry standards for registered advisers and private investment funds. Assisting with regulatory filings, including Form ADV, Form PF, and Form D, and coordinating responses to regulatory inquiries.\n\n - Handling corporate and entity matters, including forming and maintaining fund vehicles, general partner and management entities; supporting corporate governance, entity management, and maintenance of organizational records; and assisting with the company’s own corporate and commercial matters.\n\n - Drafting, negotiating, and managing various legal documents, including transaction documents, carry program documents, client agreements, vendor contracts, and NDAs, ensuring they are current and compliant.\n\n - Building and maintaining strong working relationships with key business partners, including external counsel, clients, and internal teams, to effectively support Allocate’s business initiatives.\n\n - Actively contributing to the development of Allocate’s investment and technology products and initiatives.\n\n\nQUALIFICATIONS\n\n - At least 4 years of experience at a major law firm or in-house legal department working on private funds; experience with open-ended and closed-ended funds a plus.\n\n - Juris Doctor degree from an accredited law school and at least one active bar membership/license to practice law in any state.\n\n - Strong understanding of the asset management industry and private funds, with detailed knowledge of the securities laws and regulations most relevant to private fund advisers—principally the Investment Advisers Act; the Securities Act and Regulation D (including Rule 506(b)/(c) and the accredited-investor and qualified-purchaser standards); and the Investment Company Act exclusions relied on by private funds (Sections 3(c)(1) and 3(c)(7)). Familiarity with blue-sky/Form D filings and the broker-dealer/FINRA framework is a plus.\n\n - Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to interact professionally with clients and team members.\n\n - Willingness to be very hands-on and proactive in offering solutions; comfortable with technology.\n\n - Strong organizational skills with the capability to manage multiple tasks and meet deadlines effectively, while maintaining keen attention to detail and accuracy in all work product.\n\n\nESSENTIAL VALUES & CULTURE\n\n Providing our clients with a world-class experience is our number one priority. We obsessively search for ways to improve the experience for our clients and partners. This requires extraordinary response times, proactivity, and ensuring that everything we do, from product strategy to offline communications, is a top-tier client experience.\n\n - Challenge convention: Instead of detailing all the reasons why an idea may not work, we constantly question things to determine how a viable idea may be put into motion.\n\n - Commitment to continuous improvement: We find ways to personally scale each day by pushing ourselves up the learning curve.\n\n - Meritocracy, not politics: We place the utmost value on results and rewards through merit, not reward actions driven by political agendas or behavior.\n\n - Civil Discourse is embraced: We believe open, intellectually curious conversations are required to arrive at the best decisions. Respect is paramount in our dealings with one another, but our mission is always to get the right answer collectively, not to be right.\n\n\nADDITIONAL DETAILS\n\n - Reporting to: Senior Counsel\n\n - Location: SF Bay Area, NYC, CT, or Boston preferred; all U.S. candidates will be considered. Hybrid for SF Bay Area and NY offices.\n\n - Salary Range: It is expected that the base annual salary range for this position in the locations listed above will be $180,000 - $210,000. Actual salary will be determined based on the candidate’s experience, location, skills, training, certifications and education, and other relevant qualifications specific to the role, as well as internal equity and market data. Total compensation may also include equity and discretionary performance-based bonus based on factors such as individual and team performance.\n\n - Benefits: Medical, dental, vision, responsible time off (RTO), 401k\n\n - Employment: Full-time\n\n - This role will be subject to Allocate’s Code of Ethics and related compliance obligations.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$180K – $210K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$180K - $210K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"db01e0cc-b275-4770-ba04-00c27b1044bf","tierSummary":"$180K – $210K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"b15974c9-49f3-4db7-8528-a7d721f368ab","summary":"$180K – $210K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":180000,"maxValue":210000},{"id":"a16edf24-6619-4302-83c6-643266b7ba2e","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"e9afc12f-25b7-473b-b6be-2b6ccf3fd2ac","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":180000,"maxValue":210000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"5f38e98e-f3fb-41ff-90c7-eff621c8d7fc","title":"Machine Learning Engineer","department":"Operations","team":"Insights","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-09T21:52:21.575+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Palo Alto"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/allocate/5f38e98e-f3fb-41ff-90c7-eff621c8d7fc","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/allocate/5f38e98e-f3fb-41ff-90c7-eff621c8d7fc/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>About Allocate</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Allocate is transforming private market investing by enabling RIAs and family offices to seamlessly discover, model, and manage their private market exposure. Our platform combines curated fund and co-investment opportunities with institutional-grade infrastructure. Through a single, data-rich digital experience, clients access top-tier opportunities across venture capital, private equity, private credit, and other private asset classes—backed by powerful tracking, analytics, and administration tools.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>About the Role</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Allocate is looking to add an AI / Extraction Engineer to the team! There's a lot for us to build, and we need a strong engineer with a broad skillset who can jump right in to help us lay the technical foundation for the company's future.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Essential Responsibilities and Duties</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build, train, and improve machine-learning models for production use.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop evaluation and feedback loops that measurably improve model performance over time.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stand up the tooling to measure, monitor, and track model quality.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Evaluate new models and techniques, and bring the best into production.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate cross-functionally to ship ML-powered capabilities.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Must Have Experience</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4+ years of applied ML / LLM engineering in production, with strong Python.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience taking models from prototype to reliable production systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on model fine-tuning and rigorous evaluation discipline.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficiency with Git and version control systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience with AI-assisted development tools such as Claude Code, OpenAI's Codex, or Cursor, and a demonstrated ability to incorporate new tools as they emerge.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Nice to Haves</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Applied NLP, computer vision, or multimodal models.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">MLOps and model-monitoring tooling.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Background in fintech or financial data.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Education</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, a similar technical field, or equivalent practical experience.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Essential Values &amp; Culture</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Providing our clients with a world-class experience is our number one priority.</strong> We obsessively search for ways to improve the experience for our clients and partners—extraordinary response times, proactivity, and a top-tier experience in everything from product strategy to offline communications.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Challenge convention:</strong> Instead of detailing all the reasons an idea may not work, we question things to determine how a viable idea may be put into motion.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Commitment to continuous improvement:</strong> We find ways to personally scale each day by pushing ourselves up the learning curve.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Meritocracy, not politics:</strong> We place the utmost value on results and reward through merit, not political agendas.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Civil Discourse is embraced:</strong> Open, intellectually curious conversations are required to consistently arrive at the best decisions. Respect is paramount, but the mission is to get the right answer collectively, not to be right.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Embrace technological change:</strong> We adopt tools and techniques that make us faster, smarter, and better—especially around AI and automation—and drop outdated methods without hesitation.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Additional Details</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Fully Remote (all I-9 eligible candidates will be considered).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Employment:</strong> Full-time. Seniority: Senior professional.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Salary:</strong> The expected base salary range for this role is $165,000 to $185,000. Actual compensation will be determined based on the candidate's primary work location and other job-related factors including skills, experience, qualifications, interview performance, internal equity, and market data. Candidates located in higher cost-of-living markets, including the San Francisco Bay Area, may be considered within the higher end of the range. This range reflects base salary only and does not include bonus, equity, or benefits; total compensation may also include a discretionary performance-based bonus.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Benefits:</strong> Medical, dental, and vision; 401(k); and responsible vacation time (PTO).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Travel required for team and department offsites. An in-person interview may be required during the process. A broadband internet connection is required. Compliance with Allocate's Code of Ethics is a given for this role.</p></li></ul>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT ALLOCATE\n\nAllocate is transforming private market investing by enabling RIAs and family offices to seamlessly discover, model, and manage their private market exposure. Our platform combines curated fund and co-investment opportunities with institutional-grade infrastructure. Through a single, data-rich digital experience, clients access top-tier opportunities across venture capital, private equity, private credit, and other private asset classes—backed by powerful tracking, analytics, and administration tools.\n\n\n\n\nABOUT THE ROLE\n\nAllocate is looking to add an AI / Extraction Engineer to the team! There's a lot for us to build, and we need a strong engineer with a broad skillset who can jump right in to help us lay the technical foundation for the company's future.\n\n\n\n\nESSENTIAL RESPONSIBILITIES AND DUTIES\n\n - Build, train, and improve machine-learning models for production use.\n\n - Develop evaluation and feedback loops that measurably improve model performance over time.\n\n - Stand up the tooling to measure, monitor, and track model quality.\n\n - Evaluate new models and techniques, and bring the best into production.\n\n - Collaborate cross-functionally to ship ML-powered capabilities.\n\n\nMUST HAVE EXPERIENCE\n\n - 4+ years of applied ML / LLM engineering in production, with strong Python.\n\n - Experience taking models from prototype to reliable production systems.\n\n - Hands-on model fine-tuning and rigorous evaluation discipline.\n\n - Proficiency with Git and version control systems.\n\n - Hands-on experience with AI-assisted development tools such as Claude Code, OpenAI's Codex, or Cursor, and a demonstrated ability to incorporate new tools as they emerge.\n\n\nNICE TO HAVES\n\n - Applied NLP, computer vision, or multimodal models.\n\n - MLOps and model-monitoring tooling.\n\n - Background in fintech or financial data.\n\n\nEDUCATION\n\n - Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, a similar technical field, or equivalent practical experience.\n\n\nESSENTIAL VALUES & CULTURE\n\n - Providing our clients with a world-class experience is our number one priority. We obsessively search for ways to improve the experience for our clients and partners—extraordinary response times, proactivity, and a top-tier experience in everything from product strategy to offline communications.\n\n - Challenge convention: Instead of detailing all the reasons an idea may not work, we question things to determine how a viable idea may be put into motion.\n\n - Commitment to continuous improvement: We find ways to personally scale each day by pushing ourselves up the learning curve.\n\n - Meritocracy, not politics: We place the utmost value on results and reward through merit, not political agendas.\n\n - Civil Discourse is embraced: Open, intellectually curious conversations are required to consistently arrive at the best decisions. Respect is paramount, but the mission is to get the right answer collectively, not to be right.\n\n - Embrace technological change: We adopt tools and techniques that make us faster, smarter, and better—especially around AI and automation—and drop outdated methods without hesitation.\n\n\nADDITIONAL DETAILS\n\n - Location: Fully Remote (all I-9 eligible candidates will be considered).\n\n - Employment: Full-time. Seniority: Senior professional.\n\n - Salary: The expected base salary range for this role is $165,000 to $185,000. Actual compensation will be determined based on the candidate's primary work location and other job-related factors including skills, experience, qualifications, interview performance, internal equity, and market data. Candidates located in higher cost-of-living markets, including the San Francisco Bay Area, may be considered within the higher end of the range. This range reflects base salary only and does not include bonus, equity, or benefits; total compensation may also include a discretionary performance-based bonus.\n\n - Benefits: Medical, dental, and vision; 401(k); and responsible vacation time (PTO).\n\n - Travel required for team and department offsites. An in-person interview may be required during the process. A broadband internet connection is required. Compliance with Allocate's Code of Ethics is a given for this role.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$165K – $185K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$165K - $185K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"a7a42af9-a2be-4b0b-8855-91f9d0af8e48","tierSummary":"$165K – $185K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"4e81379b-618a-4524-a589-aaf77dbbf483","summary":"$165K – $185K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":165000,"maxValue":185000},{"id":"754f1f63-eefa-419c-a6c1-872b540ef9fe","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":165000,"maxValue":185000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"228c1cf7-d257-4db6-bafd-3eca09fe19f7","title":"Senior Data Operations Analyst","department":"Operations","team":"Insights","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York Office (On-Site)","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-09T21:53:55.529+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":false,"workplaceType":"OnSite","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/allocate/228c1cf7-d257-4db6-bafd-3eca09fe19f7","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/allocate/228c1cf7-d257-4db6-bafd-3eca09fe19f7/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>About Allocate</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Allocate transforms private market investing by enabling RIAs and family offices to discover, model, and manage their private market exposure. The platform provides curated fund and co-investment opportunities with institutional-grade infrastructure across venture capital, private equity, private credit, and other private asset classes.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>The Opportunity</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Private market data is messy. It arrives as unstructured documents from hundreds of managers and fund administrators in no consistent format, and it spans both the pre-investment picture — fund terms, manager and vehicle characteristics, track record — and post-investment reporting: capital account statements, capital calls, distributions, financial statements and tax documents.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role owns data as a system across all of it, not a single dataset or a single product line: the fund and entity master, the checks that catch problems before clients do, the reconciliation that proves the numbers tie, and the analysis that explains where data is wrong and why. It is a broad remit</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The work is equal parts investigation and design. You will spend as much time working out why something broke as you will building the thing that stops it breaking again.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What You'll Own</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• <strong>Data as a system, across every product line. </strong>A consistent, governed view of funds, entities and positions that holds up wherever it is consumed — operated vehicles, administered funds, and client-held positions alike.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• <strong>Fund and entity data quality — the security master. </strong>Fund and manager records, entity resolution and duplicates, fund properties and characteristics.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• <strong>Data quality and completeness. </strong>Design and run the checks that validate data before it reaches clients, and the exception workflows behind them.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• <strong>Reconciliation. </strong>Reconcile data across our systems and sources, and explain the differences clearly.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• <strong>Root-cause analysis. </strong>Trace a wrong number back to its source, size the problem, and specify the fix.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• <strong>Extraction quality. </strong>Expand the data we capture and evaluate how well our tooling captures it.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• <strong>Documentation. </strong>Definitions, assumptions and edge cases, written down and kept current.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Must Have Experience</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• 3+ years in data operations, reference or master data, fund operations, or financial operations</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Basic SQL</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Hands-on data reconciliation experience</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Experience designing or operating data quality checks, validation rules or exception workflows</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• A process improvement mindset — you would rather fix the cause than clear the queue faster</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Comfortable in a startup environment: ambiguity, shifting priorities, and limited existing process</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Detail-oriented, with strong, consistent judgment under SLAs</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Comfort with data and modern software, including AI-assisted tools</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Nice To Haves</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Proficient SQL</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Python for data analysis</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Security master or reference data management experience (instrument, entity or fund master)</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Entity matching or entity resolution — canonical entities, deduplication and merge review</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Data modeling — dimensional modeling, dbt, or data warehouse concepts</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Private markets experience, particularly fluency with capital account statements, capital calls, distributions, schedules of investments and K-1s</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Prompt engineering, or evaluating model extraction output against golden datasets</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• BI tooling — Metabase, Looker, Tableau or similar</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Education</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Bachelor's degree, or equivalent practical experience</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Compensation &amp; Benefits</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• <strong>Salary: </strong>$95,000–$135,000 base, plus potential discretionary bonus and equity. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• <strong>Benefits: </strong>Medical, dental, vision, 401(k), and responsible vacation time</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Values &amp; Culture</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Allocate prioritizes world-class client experiences, welcomes unconventional thinking, emphasizes continuous learning, operates on meritocracy, encourages civil discourse, and embraces technological innovation and automation.</p>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT ALLOCATE\n\nAllocate transforms private market investing by enabling RIAs and family offices to discover, model, and manage their private market exposure. The platform provides curated fund and co-investment opportunities with institutional-grade infrastructure across venture capital, private equity, private credit, and other private asset classes.\n\nThe Opportunity\n\nPrivate market data is messy. It arrives as unstructured documents from hundreds of managers and fund administrators in no consistent format, and it spans both the pre-investment picture — fund terms, manager and vehicle characteristics, track record — and post-investment reporting: capital account statements, capital calls, distributions, financial statements and tax documents.\n\nThis role owns data as a system across all of it, not a single dataset or a single product line: the fund and entity master, the checks that catch problems before clients do, the reconciliation that proves the numbers tie, and the analysis that explains where data is wrong and why. It is a broad remit\n\nThe work is equal parts investigation and design. You will spend as much time working out why something broke as you will building the thing that stops it breaking again.\n\nWhat You'll Own\n\n• Data as a system, across every product line. A consistent, governed view of funds, entities and positions that holds up wherever it is consumed — operated vehicles, administered funds, and client-held positions alike.\n\n• Fund and entity data quality — the security master. Fund and manager records, entity resolution and duplicates, fund properties and characteristics.\n\n• Data quality and completeness. Design and run the checks that validate data before it reaches clients, and the exception workflows behind them.\n\n• Reconciliation. Reconcile data across our systems and sources, and explain the differences clearly.\n\n• Root-cause analysis. Trace a wrong number back to its source, size the problem, and specify the fix.\n\n• Extraction quality. Expand the data we capture and evaluate how well our tooling captures it.\n\n• Documentation. Definitions, assumptions and edge cases, written down and kept current.\n\nMust Have Experience\n\n• 3+ years in data operations, reference or master data, fund operations, or financial operations\n\n• Basic SQL\n\n• Hands-on data reconciliation experience\n\n• Experience designing or operating data quality checks, validation rules or exception workflows\n\n• A process improvement mindset — you would rather fix the cause than clear the queue faster\n\n• Comfortable in a startup environment: ambiguity, shifting priorities, and limited existing process\n\n• Detail-oriented, with strong, consistent judgment under SLAs\n\n• Comfort with data and modern software, including AI-assisted tools\n\nNice To Haves\n\n• Proficient SQL\n\n• Python for data analysis\n\n• Security master or reference data management experience (instrument, entity or fund master)\n\n• Entity matching or entity resolution — canonical entities, deduplication and merge review\n\n• Data modeling — dimensional modeling, dbt, or data warehouse concepts\n\n• Private markets experience, particularly fluency with capital account statements, capital calls, distributions, schedules of investments and K-1s\n\n• Prompt engineering, or evaluating model extraction output against golden datasets\n\n• BI tooling — Metabase, Looker, Tableau or similar\n\nEducation\n\n• Bachelor's degree, or equivalent practical experience\n\nCompensation & Benefits\n\n• Salary: $95,000–$135,000 base, plus potential discretionary bonus and equity. \n\n• Benefits: Medical, dental, vision, 401(k), and responsible vacation time\n\nValues & Culture\n\nAllocate prioritizes world-class client experiences, welcomes unconventional thinking, emphasizes continuous learning, operates on meritocracy, encourages civil discourse, and embraces technological innovation and automation.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$95K – $135K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$95K - $135K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"49e4fe1c-bd39-406c-bd23-86aa8c905ef8","tierSummary":"$95K – $135K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"fc367bca-c4a9-4534-a36a-684b5e7d127d","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"f04fcc12-a14a-473a-8959-83172ff2e33f","summary":"$95K – $135K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":95000,"maxValue":135000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":95000,"maxValue":135000}]}},{"id":"5a321008-2fd4-476b-8d6b-7abe91c5e7b5","title":"Senior Technical Project Manager","department":"Product","team":"Product","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-27T16:36:38.717+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Palo Alto"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/allocate/5a321008-2fd4-476b-8d6b-7abe91c5e7b5","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/allocate/5a321008-2fd4-476b-8d6b-7abe91c5e7b5/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Allocate is modernizing private markets, making alternative investments more accessible and streamlined for wealth advisory firms and family offices. Backed by leading firms and driven by a mission to remove barriers in private market investing, we leverage over 100 years of collective experience to transform the industry.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are building an <strong>AI-native product organization</strong> that moves extremely fast — from idea → prototype → client feedback → production in days, not months.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">To do that well, we need a <strong>force multiplier and builder</strong>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Your Mission</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Increase the velocity of the product organization.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will sit at the center of product, engineering, design, and leadership — identifying friction, removing blockers, accelerating decisions, and compressing feedback loops so the team can move faster without losing quality.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is <strong>not a traditional project management role</strong>. Instead, you will operate as a <strong>technical operator inside the product organization</strong>, helping ideas move from concept to shipped product as quickly and smoothly as possible.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will work <strong>alongside makers — not above them</strong>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>What Success Looks Like</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Within your first few months, the team should feel noticeably faster.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work that used to take weeks happens in days. Blockers disappear before they slow the team down. Engineers, designers, and product managers spend more time building and less time coordinating.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Leadership has visibility into what’s happening without needing constant status meetings.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You identify friction in the system and remove it. You introduce tools, workflows, and habits that compound the team’s effectiveness over time.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">When something slows the team down, you don’t wait for permission to fix it.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Your impact is simple:</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>The team ships better products faster than before you joined.</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>What You’ll Be Doing</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Accelerate delivery</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive rapid feedback loops between prototyping, client input, and production — compressing weeks into days.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Keep multiple parallel workstreams moving without creating bottlenecks or bureaucracy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify what's blocking a maker and remove it — same day.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Keep leadership and key stakeholders informed with signal, not noise: what shipped, what's at risk, what needs a decision.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Act as a force multiplier for the team</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Create clarity and momentum in ambiguous environments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify and surface risks and cross-team dependencies before they become problems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Protect the team’s focus so builders can build.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help the team prioritize the work that matters most right now.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Eliminate coordination overhead wherever possible.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Be a builder</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Treat process as a product — continuously improving it as the team evolves.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Use AI tools (Cursor, v0, Claude, etc.) to prototype, draft specs, generate briefs, and unblock the team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute directly to delivery rather than only coordinating others.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Continuously experiment with new AI tooling and share what works across the team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify where AI can eliminate manual coordination overhead and implement it.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Help scale the organization</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Evolve tools and workflows as the team grows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build lightweight systems that improve alignment without slowing teams down.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ensure distributed teams communicate effectively across time zones.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Continuously look for ways to increase the speed and effectiveness of the product organization.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"> <strong>What You Bring</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is for you if you have:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience shipping real products in <strong>fast-moving startup environments</strong>; early-stage startup experience strongly preferred.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A <strong>maker mindset</strong> — you would rather prototype a solution than write a slide deck about it.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong familiarity with <strong>modern AI tooling</strong> and curiosity about how it changes how teams build software.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You are comfortable using AI tools in your daily workflow to improve productivity and coordination.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong judgment about when to move fast and when to slow down — and the credibility to call it either way.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The ability to hold context across business, product, design, and engineering without requiring rigid handoff processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communication skills — async-first, direct, and oriented toward decisions rather than status updates.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort operating in ambiguity; you create structure rather than waiting for it.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">High ownership and accountability — when something is stuck, you make it move.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with distributed teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A Bachelor’s degree. Studies in Computer Science, Engineering, Business, or a related field (or equivalent experience) would be helpful.</p></li></ul><h2>This role may not be for you if:</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You prefer structured environments where responsibilities are narrowly defined — we are a start-up and roles flex to deliver business goals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You are uncomfortable experimenting with AI tooling to improve how teams operate — we are AI-native and heavily leverage AI tools to accelerate growth.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You prefer well-defined roadmaps and long planning cycles — we are a nimble organization, and priorities change quickly.</p></li></ul><h2> Our Values &amp; Culture:</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Providing our clients with a world-class experience is our number one priority. We obsessively search for ways to improve the experience for our clients and partners. This requires extraordinary response times, proactivity, and ensuring that everything we do, from product strategy to offline communications, is a top-tier client experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Challenge convention: Instead of detailing why an idea may not work, we constantly question things to determine how a viable idea may be implemented.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Commitment to continuous improvement: We find ways to personally scale each day by pushing ourselves up the learning curve.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Meritocracy, not politics: We place the utmost value on results and rewards through merit, not reward actions driven by political agendas or behavior.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Civil Discourse is embraced: Open, intellectually curious conversations are required to make the best decisions. Respect is paramount in our dealings, but our mission is always to get the correct answer collectively.</p></li></ul><h2>Compensation, Benefits &amp; Other Details:</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Location: Remote</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reports to the Lead Technical Project Manager</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Base Salary Range: $155,000-$170,000</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Actual salary will be determined based on the candidate’s experience, location, skills, training, certifications, and education, other relevant qualifications specific to the role, and internal equity and market data. Total compensation may include equity and discretionary performance-based bonuses based on individual, team, and company performance factors.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Benefits: Medical, dental, vision, responsible time off (RTO), 401K</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Employment: Full-time</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role will be subject to Allocate's Code of Ethics and related compliance obligations of Allocate.</p></li></ul>","descriptionPlain":"Allocate is modernizing private markets, making alternative investments more accessible and streamlined for wealth advisory firms and family offices. Backed by leading firms and driven by a mission to remove barriers in private market investing, we leverage over 100 years of collective experience to transform the industry.\n\nWe are building an AI-native product organization that moves extremely fast — from idea → prototype → client feedback → production in days, not months.\n\nTo do that well, we need a force multiplier and builder.\n\n\n\n\nYOUR MISSION\n\nIncrease the velocity of the product organization.\n\nYou will sit at the center of product, engineering, design, and leadership — identifying friction, removing blockers, accelerating decisions, and compressing feedback loops so the team can move faster without losing quality.\n\nThis is not a traditional project management role. Instead, you will operate as a technical operator inside the product organization, helping ideas move from concept to shipped product as quickly and smoothly as possible.\n\nYou will work alongside makers — not above them.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT SUCCESS LOOKS LIKE\n\nWithin your first few months, the team should feel noticeably faster.\n\nWork that used to take weeks happens in days. Blockers disappear before they slow the team down. Engineers, designers, and product managers spend more time building and less time coordinating.\n\nLeadership has visibility into what’s happening without needing constant status meetings.\n\nYou identify friction in the system and remove it. You introduce tools, workflows, and habits that compound the team’s effectiveness over time.\n\nWhen something slows the team down, you don’t wait for permission to fix it.\n\nYour impact is simple:\n\nThe team ships better products faster than before you joined.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL BE DOING\n\nAccelerate delivery\n\n - Drive rapid feedback loops between prototyping, client input, and production — compressing weeks into days.\n\n - Keep multiple parallel workstreams moving without creating bottlenecks or bureaucracy.\n\n - Identify what's blocking a maker and remove it — same day.\n\n - Keep leadership and key stakeholders informed with signal, not noise: what shipped, what's at risk, what needs a decision.\n\nAct as a force multiplier for the team\n\n - Create clarity and momentum in ambiguous environments.\n\n - Identify and surface risks and cross-team dependencies before they become problems.\n\n - Protect the team’s focus so builders can build.\n\n - Help the team prioritize the work that matters most right now.\n\n - Eliminate coordination overhead wherever possible.\n\nBe a builder\n\n - Treat process as a product — continuously improving it as the team evolves.\n\n - Use AI tools (Cursor, v0, Claude, etc.) to prototype, draft specs, generate briefs, and unblock the team.\n\n - Contribute directly to delivery rather than only coordinating others.\n\n - Continuously experiment with new AI tooling and share what works across the team.\n\n - Identify where AI can eliminate manual coordination overhead and implement it.\n\nHelp scale the organization\n\n - Evolve tools and workflows as the team grows.\n\n - Build lightweight systems that improve alignment without slowing teams down.\n\n - Ensure distributed teams communicate effectively across time zones.\n\n - Continuously look for ways to increase the speed and effectiveness of the product organization.\n\n What You Bring\n\nThis role is for you if you have:\n\n - Experience shipping real products in fast-moving startup environments; early-stage startup experience strongly preferred.\n\n - A maker mindset — you would rather prototype a solution than write a slide deck about it.\n\n - Strong familiarity with modern AI tooling and curiosity about how it changes how teams build software.\n\n - You are comfortable using AI tools in your daily workflow to improve productivity and coordination.\n\n - Strong judgment about when to move fast and when to slow down — and the credibility to call it either way.\n\n - The ability to hold context across business, product, design, and engineering without requiring rigid handoff processes.\n\n - Excellent communication skills — async-first, direct, and oriented toward decisions rather than status updates.\n\n - Comfort operating in ambiguity; you create structure rather than waiting for it.\n\n - High ownership and accountability — when something is stuck, you make it move.\n\n - Experience working with distributed teams.\n\n - A Bachelor’s degree. Studies in Computer Science, Engineering, Business, or a related field (or equivalent experience) would be helpful.\n\n\nTHIS ROLE MAY NOT BE FOR YOU IF:\n\n - You prefer structured environments where responsibilities are narrowly defined — we are a start-up and roles flex to deliver business goals.\n\n - You are uncomfortable experimenting with AI tooling to improve how teams operate — we are AI-native and heavily leverage AI tools to accelerate growth.\n\n - You prefer well-defined roadmaps and long planning cycles — we are a nimble organization, and priorities change quickly.\n\n\n OUR VALUES & CULTURE:\n\n - Providing our clients with a world-class experience is our number one priority. We obsessively search for ways to improve the experience for our clients and partners. This requires extraordinary response times, proactivity, and ensuring that everything we do, from product strategy to offline communications, is a top-tier client experience.\n\n - Challenge convention: Instead of detailing why an idea may not work, we constantly question things to determine how a viable idea may be implemented.\n\n - Commitment to continuous improvement: We find ways to personally scale each day by pushing ourselves up the learning curve.\n\n - Meritocracy, not politics: We place the utmost value on results and rewards through merit, not reward actions driven by political agendas or behavior.\n\n - Civil Discourse is embraced: Open, intellectually curious conversations are required to make the best decisions. Respect is paramount in our dealings, but our mission is always to get the correct answer collectively.\n\n\nCOMPENSATION, BENEFITS & OTHER DETAILS:\n\n - Location: Remote\n\n - Reports to the Lead Technical Project Manager\n\n - Base Salary Range: $155,000-$170,000\n\n - Actual salary will be determined based on the candidate’s experience, location, skills, training, certifications, and education, other relevant qualifications specific to the role, and internal equity and market data. Total compensation may include equity and discretionary performance-based bonuses based on individual, team, and company performance factors.\n\n - Benefits: Medical, dental, vision, responsible time off (RTO), 401K\n\n - Employment: Full-time\n\n - This role will be subject to Allocate's Code of Ethics and related compliance obligations of Allocate.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$155K – $175K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$155K - $175K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"e6ea8b44-76be-4827-9fac-44d7a4f5e1cb","tierSummary":"$155K – $175K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"195c56be-5409-4705-9da7-8c75131f899a","summary":"$155K – $175K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":155000,"maxValue":175000},{"id":"d516a028-c6e2-4adf-b3cd-2aad112007ad","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":155000,"maxValue":175000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"3ecfc6fd-27b9-4e85-82dc-8bde54be51fe","title":"Revenue Manager","department":"Accounting","team":"Accounting","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Palo Alto Office (Hybrid)","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-06T18:10:24.153+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Palo Alto"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/allocate/3ecfc6fd-27b9-4e85-82dc-8bde54be51fe","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/allocate/3ecfc6fd-27b9-4e85-82dc-8bde54be51fe/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>About Allocate</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Allocate is building the operating system for private markets. Our platform gives wealth advisors, family offices, and qualified individuals streamlined access to institutional-quality venture capital, private equity, and private credit funds — automating fund discovery, subscription, and portfolio management. Since launch, Allocate has scaled to over $5 billion on the platform, serving more than 550 wealth advisory firms and institutional family offices.</p><h2><strong>The Role</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Allocate is looking for a Revenue Manager to own revenue recognition and billing operations for a fast-scaling fintech platform. This role owns the revenue close process end to end, ensures billing data integrity across Salesforce and downstream systems, and builds the scalable processes, controls, and team Allocate needs as transaction volume and product complexity grow. This is a hands-on role with significant ownership and visibility into the finance function, reporting to the Controller.</p><h2><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the end-to-end revenue recognition process in accordance with ASC 606, including contract review, deferred revenue schedules, and revenue journal entries.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage the billing lifecycle from contract and order through invoicing, ensuring accuracy across Salesforce and downstream billing systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with RevOps and Engineering to build, organize and maintain clean, well-structured revenue and billing data across databases and systems of record.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and implement scalable billing processes and controls to support Allocate’s growing transaction volume and evolving product structures.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own revenue-related account reconciliations (deferred revenue, accounts receivable, unbilled revenue) and the monthly and quarterly close for revenue.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Sales, Legal, and Product to review new contract structures and ensure appropriate revenue treatment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify and implement automation opportunities to reduce manual revenue and billing work as volume scales.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assist in preparation for the first external audit, including preparation of schedules and policy documentation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead technical accounting research and memo preparation for new or complex revenue arrangements.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner closely with Controller on implementation of a new ERP for multiple entity structure.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>What We’re Looking For</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bachelor’s degree in Accounting, Finance, or a related field. CPA preferred.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">6+ years of progressive accounting experience with a focus on revenue recognition and billing, ideally in a SaaS or fintech environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prior experience managing or mentoring staff, or readiness to take on people management as the team grows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Solid working knowledge of ASC 606 and SaaS revenue recognition best practices.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience with Salesforce (or a similar CRM/CPQ) and its interplay with billing and revenue systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in system implementations, SQL, databasis and revenue systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort organizing and working across databases, with the ability to query, reconcile, and troubleshoot data across systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record of scaling billing processes and systems to support company growth.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong Excel skills and comfort working with large data sets.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communication skills and the ability to work cross-functionally with Sales, RevOps, Engineering, and external auditors.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fund accounting experience is a plus.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Why Allocate</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The opportunity to build and lead revenue and billing infrastructure at a high-growth fintech company reshaping private markets.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Direct partnership with the Controller and broader leadership.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A hybrid work environment in Palo Alto, CA</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comprehensive benefits, including health coverage, equity, and paid time off.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Base salary range: $135,000 – $160,000 plus equity and benefits. Final offer will be based on experience and location.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>How to Apply</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Interested candidates should submit a resume and brief cover letter outlining relevant experience. Allocate is an equal opportunity employer committed to building a diverse and inclusive team.</p>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT ALLOCATE\n\nAllocate is building the operating system for private markets. Our platform gives wealth advisors, family offices, and qualified individuals streamlined access to institutional-quality venture capital, private equity, and private credit funds — automating fund discovery, subscription, and portfolio management. Since launch, Allocate has scaled to over $5 billion on the platform, serving more than 550 wealth advisory firms and institutional family offices.\n\n\nTHE ROLE\n\nAllocate is looking for a Revenue Manager to own revenue recognition and billing operations for a fast-scaling fintech platform. This role owns the revenue close process end to end, ensures billing data integrity across Salesforce and downstream systems, and builds the scalable processes, controls, and team Allocate needs as transaction volume and product complexity grow. This is a hands-on role with significant ownership and visibility into the finance function, reporting to the Controller.\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Own the end-to-end revenue recognition process in accordance with ASC 606, including contract review, deferred revenue schedules, and revenue journal entries.\n\n - Manage the billing lifecycle from contract and order through invoicing, ensuring accuracy across Salesforce and downstream billing systems.\n\n - Partner with RevOps and Engineering to build, organize and maintain clean, well-structured revenue and billing data across databases and systems of record.\n\n - Design and implement scalable billing processes and controls to support Allocate’s growing transaction volume and evolving product structures.\n\n - Own revenue-related account reconciliations (deferred revenue, accounts receivable, unbilled revenue) and the monthly and quarterly close for revenue.\n\n - Partner with Sales, Legal, and Product to review new contract structures and ensure appropriate revenue treatment.\n\n - Identify and implement automation opportunities to reduce manual revenue and billing work as volume scales.\n\n - Assist in preparation for the first external audit, including preparation of schedules and policy documentation.\n\n - Lead technical accounting research and memo preparation for new or complex revenue arrangements.\n\n - Partner closely with Controller on implementation of a new ERP for multiple entity structure.\n\n\nWHAT WE’RE LOOKING FOR\n\n - Bachelor’s degree in Accounting, Finance, or a related field. CPA preferred.\n\n - 6+ years of progressive accounting experience with a focus on revenue recognition and billing, ideally in a SaaS or fintech environment.\n\n - Prior experience managing or mentoring staff, or readiness to take on people management as the team grows.\n\n - Solid working knowledge of ASC 606 and SaaS revenue recognition best practices.\n\n - Hands-on experience with Salesforce (or a similar CRM/CPQ) and its interplay with billing and revenue systems.\n\n - Experience in system implementations, SQL, databasis and revenue systems.\n\n - Comfort organizing and working across databases, with the ability to query, reconcile, and troubleshoot data across systems.\n\n - A track record of scaling billing processes and systems to support company growth.\n\n - Strong Excel skills and comfort working with large data sets.\n\n - Excellent communication skills and the ability to work cross-functionally with Sales, RevOps, Engineering, and external auditors.\n\n - Fund accounting experience is a plus.\n\n\nWHY ALLOCATE\n\n - The opportunity to build and lead revenue and billing infrastructure at a high-growth fintech company reshaping private markets.\n\n - Direct partnership with the Controller and broader leadership.\n\n - A hybrid work environment in Palo Alto, CA\n\n - Comprehensive benefits, including health coverage, equity, and paid time off.\n\n - Base salary range: $135,000 – $160,000 plus equity and benefits. Final offer will be based on experience and location.\n\n\nHOW TO APPLY\n\nInterested candidates should submit a resume and brief cover letter outlining relevant experience. Allocate is an equal opportunity employer committed to building a diverse and inclusive team.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$135K – $160K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$135K - $160K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"8e56120d-0c06-44c8-9fd7-b15a6d9191ac","tierSummary":"$135K – $160K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"5f22b4fb-898b-4af2-a18b-3ab7bacd4601","summary":"$135K – $160K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":135000,"maxValue":160000},{"id":"43f4a9c6-162b-44c1-af3e-bebac7e8469e","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":135000,"maxValue":160000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"1b7d63da-215d-478b-b7a0-4bc5e76a977d","title":"Head of Design","department":"Design","team":"Design","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Palo Alto Office (Hybrid)","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-18T17:56:59.980+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Palo Alto"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/allocate/1b7d63da-215d-478b-b7a0-4bc5e76a977d","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/allocate/1b7d63da-215d-478b-b7a0-4bc5e76a977d/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1>About Allocate</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Allocate is building the operating system for private markets — wealth advisors and their clients use the platform to access, transact in, and manage private market investments. The platform supports 350+ advisory firms and 1,500+ GP relationships, with $ 5B+ in assets on the platform.</p><h1>About The Role</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This position owns and builds the design function at Allocate, reporting directly to the CEO and working in lockstep with product and engineering leadership.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a build role, not a caretaking one. A small team, a working design system, and a live product are already in place. The mandate is to take all three further: set the standard, grow the team, and decide what design owns and how it earns that ownership.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The role stays hands-on by design. At this stage, the person leading design is still in the work: shaping the hardest flows, prototyping the ideas that must be seen to be understood, sitting in the details when the details matter.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">One thing is non-negotiable: this role starts from the client and works backward. Engineering constraints are inputs to negotiate, not the frame to design inside. The right person asks what will provide advisors and fund managers a great product experience.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Private markets are dense — funds, co-investments, capital calls, distributions, portfolio reporting. This is the one area where the company isn't hiring someone to learn on the job. Candidates need to already speak this language, because <em>“the difference between a good interface and a great one is knowing what the numbers actually mean to the person reading them.”</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design currently runs on Figma, Magic Patterns, and Anthropic, moving fast from idea to interactive prototype, validating with stakeholders and users, and cutting engineering risk before development starts. Fluency with this workflow is expected, not optional.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>WHY THIS ROLE MATTERS</strong></em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design is where Allocate's complexity becomes either clarity or friction. In a space this nuanced, a great interface isn't polished on top of the problem — it's <em>“the difference between a client trusting the platform with real capital and bouncing off it.”</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The same is true of the brand. Allocate's clients are advisors and family offices deciding whether to move real money through the platform, and every surface either earns that trust or spends it. One person holding a product, system, and brand is how those surfaces start telling the same story.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Impact compounds here — in the quality bar set, the system strengthened, and the designers who level up because of who was leading them.</p><h1>What You’ll Own</h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Product design across Allocate — the advisor and GP experience, unified and end-to-end</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Private markets knowledge, applied directly and deepened continuously, so decisions are grounded in understanding rather than assumption</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The quality bar, held with real mechanisms, not vibes: a clear definition of done, pre-launch usability gates, a standing view of friction in the live product</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The hardest problems, end to end — research, framing, prototyping, handoff</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The team — hire, define levels and growth paths, coach through feedback, reviews, and 1:1s</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The roadmap, alongside product and engineering leadership — defining problems well, forcing tradeoffs early rather than at handoff</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A seat in product strategy, not just product execution — design's voice in executive conversations, framed around client value and business outcomes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The design system — consistency as the default, speed as the byproduct</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Brand expression across the marketing site, campaigns, launch moments, and client-facing collateral</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A validation habit built for this size: fast, evidence-led, prototype-first, actually used</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">AI-assisted tools for research synthesis, exploration, and prototyping — freeing the team for the judgment, taste, and craft only people bring</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">How design works with the rest of the company — rituals, tooling, process, added only where they earn their keep</p></li></ul><h1>Who You Are</h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">10+ years in product design, several of them leading and managing designers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Have built or substantially grown a design function — hiring, leveling, coaching, setting practice, not just running a queue</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Led distributed designers and held craft and cohesion high without needing to be in the same room</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Still hands-on, and want to stay that way — looking for a role where leading and making are the same job</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong systems thinker, with a design system carried through real growth</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable across product and brand — may lean one way, but can hold both and know when each is the lever</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Direct experience designing for private markets, or an adjacent institutional finance domain dense enough to demand real mastery — fund structures, capital calls, distributions, and portfolio reporting are already familiar ground</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prototype-first: fluent in Figma and Magic Patterns, ready to build in Claude when code is the fastest path — not an engineer, but rarely blocked by code</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Pragmatic and experiment-friendly — multiple options, early validation, evidence over opinion</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong collaborator with engineers, PMs, and stakeholders — clear and flexible</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A strong communicator and storyteller — in a 1:1, an exec room, or in front of clients</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Based in the Bay Area, or ready to be — this role is in the Palo Alto office</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>WHY THIS IS WORTH YOUR TIME</strong></em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is the role for someone who wants to own design at a company building something new: leading the work, shaping the system, defining the brand, and building the team — while turning one of finance's most complex corners into something people actually want to use. And at this stage, the person who owns how clients experience Allocate has a real voice in what Allocate becomes.</p><h1>Essential Values &amp; Culture</h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Providing our clients with a world-class experience is our number one priority. We obsessively search for ways to improve the experience for our clients and partners. This requires extraordinary response times, proactivity, and ensuring that everything we do — from product strategy to offline communications — reflects a top-tier client experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Challenge convention: Instead of detailing all the reasons why an idea may not work, we constantly question things to determine how a viable idea may be put into motion.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Commitment to continuous improvement: We find ways to personally scale each day by pushing ourselves up the learning curve.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Meritocracy, not politics: We place the utmost value on results and rewards through merit, not reward actions driven by political agendas or behavior.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Civil Discourse is embraced: We believe open, intellectually curious conversations are required to consistently arrive at the best decisions. Respect is paramount in our dealings with one another, but our mission is always to get the right answer collectively, not to be right.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Embrace technological change: We adopt tools and techniques that make us faster, smarter, and better. We stay open to innovation, especially around AI and automation, and drop outdated methods without hesitation. This includes actively integrating AI-assisted tools into your daily workflow and staying current as the landscape evolves. Complacency kills progress — we value adaptability and curiosity.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>Additional Details</h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hybrid Position - 3 days/week in Palo Alto office required</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Travel may be required for company offsites</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Broadband internet connection required</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Location: All I-9 eligible candidates will be considered</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Salary: $225,000 - $260,000+ base, with bonus and equity eligibility</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Benefits: Medical, dental, and vision; 401(k); and responsible vacation time (PTO)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Employment: Full-time</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reports to: CEO and Co-Founder</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>The base pay offered will be determined based on the candidate's experience, location, skills, training, certifications, education, internal equity, and market data. Total compensation may also include a discretionary performance-based bonus. We do not anticipate that candidates hired will begin at the top of the range or above, though this may occur on a case-by-case basis.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT ALLOCATE\n\nAllocate is building the operating system for private markets — wealth advisors and their clients use the platform to access, transact in, and manage private market investments. The platform supports 350+ advisory firms and 1,500+ GP relationships, with $ 5B+ in assets on the platform.\n\n\nABOUT THE ROLE\n\nThis position owns and builds the design function at Allocate, reporting directly to the CEO and working in lockstep with product and engineering leadership.\n\nThis is a build role, not a caretaking one. A small team, a working design system, and a live product are already in place. The mandate is to take all three further: set the standard, grow the team, and decide what design owns and how it earns that ownership.\n\nThe role stays hands-on by design. At this stage, the person leading design is still in the work: shaping the hardest flows, prototyping the ideas that must be seen to be understood, sitting in the details when the details matter.\n\nOne thing is non-negotiable: this role starts from the client and works backward. Engineering constraints are inputs to negotiate, not the frame to design inside. The right person asks what will provide advisors and fund managers a great product experience.\n\nPrivate markets are dense — funds, co-investments, capital calls, distributions, portfolio reporting. This is the one area where the company isn't hiring someone to learn on the job. Candidates need to already speak this language, because “the difference between a good interface and a great one is knowing what the numbers actually mean to the person reading them.”\n\nDesign currently runs on Figma, Magic Patterns, and Anthropic, moving fast from idea to interactive prototype, validating with stakeholders and users, and cutting engineering risk before development starts. Fluency with this workflow is expected, not optional.\n\nWHY THIS ROLE MATTERS\n\nDesign is where Allocate's complexity becomes either clarity or friction. In a space this nuanced, a great interface isn't polished on top of the problem — it's “the difference between a client trusting the platform with real capital and bouncing off it.”\n\nThe same is true of the brand. Allocate's clients are advisors and family offices deciding whether to move real money through the platform, and every surface either earns that trust or spends it. One person holding a product, system, and brand is how those surfaces start telling the same story.\n\nImpact compounds here — in the quality bar set, the system strengthened, and the designers who level up because of who was leading them.\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL OWN\n\n - Product design across Allocate — the advisor and GP experience, unified and end-to-end\n\n - Private markets knowledge, applied directly and deepened continuously, so decisions are grounded in understanding rather than assumption\n\n - The quality bar, held with real mechanisms, not vibes: a clear definition of done, pre-launch usability gates, a standing view of friction in the live product\n\n - The hardest problems, end to end — research, framing, prototyping, handoff\n\n - The team — hire, define levels and growth paths, coach through feedback, reviews, and 1:1s\n\n - The roadmap, alongside product and engineering leadership — defining problems well, forcing tradeoffs early rather than at handoff\n\n - A seat in product strategy, not just product execution — design's voice in executive conversations, framed around client value and business outcomes\n\n - The design system — consistency as the default, speed as the byproduct\n\n - Brand expression across the marketing site, campaigns, launch moments, and client-facing collateral\n\n - A validation habit built for this size: fast, evidence-led, prototype-first, actually used\n\n - AI-assisted tools for research synthesis, exploration, and prototyping — freeing the team for the judgment, taste, and craft only people bring\n\n - How design works with the rest of the company — rituals, tooling, process, added only where they earn their keep\n\n\nWHO YOU ARE\n\n - 10+ years in product design, several of them leading and managing designers\n\n - Have built or substantially grown a design function — hiring, leveling, coaching, setting practice, not just running a queue\n\n - Led distributed designers and held craft and cohesion high without needing to be in the same room\n\n - Still hands-on, and want to stay that way — looking for a role where leading and making are the same job\n\n - Strong systems thinker, with a design system carried through real growth\n\n - Comfortable across product and brand — may lean one way, but can hold both and know when each is the lever\n\n - Direct experience designing for private markets, or an adjacent institutional finance domain dense enough to demand real mastery — fund structures, capital calls, distributions, and portfolio reporting are already familiar ground\n\n - Prototype-first: fluent in Figma and Magic Patterns, ready to build in Claude when code is the fastest path — not an engineer, but rarely blocked by code\n\n - Pragmatic and experiment-friendly — multiple options, early validation, evidence over opinion\n\n - Strong collaborator with engineers, PMs, and stakeholders — clear and flexible\n\n - A strong communicator and storyteller — in a 1:1, an exec room, or in front of clients\n\n - Based in the Bay Area, or ready to be — this role is in the Palo Alto office\n\nWHY THIS IS WORTH YOUR TIME\n\nThis is the role for someone who wants to own design at a company building something new: leading the work, shaping the system, defining the brand, and building the team — while turning one of finance's most complex corners into something people actually want to use. And at this stage, the person who owns how clients experience Allocate has a real voice in what Allocate becomes.\n\n\nESSENTIAL VALUES & CULTURE\n\n - Providing our clients with a world-class experience is our number one priority. We obsessively search for ways to improve the experience for our clients and partners. This requires extraordinary response times, proactivity, and ensuring that everything we do — from product strategy to offline communications — reflects a top-tier client experience.\n\n - Challenge convention: Instead of detailing all the reasons why an idea may not work, we constantly question things to determine how a viable idea may be put into motion.\n\n - Commitment to continuous improvement: We find ways to personally scale each day by pushing ourselves up the learning curve.\n\n - Meritocracy, not politics: We place the utmost value on results and rewards through merit, not reward actions driven by political agendas or behavior.\n\n - Civil Discourse is embraced: We believe open, intellectually curious conversations are required to consistently arrive at the best decisions. Respect is paramount in our dealings with one another, but our mission is always to get the right answer collectively, not to be right.\n\n - Embrace technological change: We adopt tools and techniques that make us faster, smarter, and better. We stay open to innovation, especially around AI and automation, and drop outdated methods without hesitation. This includes actively integrating AI-assisted tools into your daily workflow and staying current as the landscape evolves. Complacency kills progress — we value adaptability and curiosity.\n\n\n\n\nADDITIONAL DETAILS\n\n - Hybrid Position - 3 days/week in Palo Alto office required\n\n - Travel may be required for company offsites\n\n - Broadband internet connection required\n\n - Location: All I-9 eligible candidates will be considered\n\n - Salary: $225,000 - $260,000+ base, with bonus and equity eligibility\n\n - Benefits: Medical, dental, and vision; 401(k); and responsible vacation time (PTO)\n\n - Employment: Full-time\n\n - Reports to: CEO and Co-Founder\n\n\n\nThe base pay offered will be determined based on the candidate's experience, location, skills, training, certifications, education, internal equity, and market data. Total compensation may also include a discretionary performance-based bonus. We do not anticipate that candidates hired will begin at the top of the range or above, though this may occur on a case-by-case basis.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$225K – $260K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$225K - $260K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"2309a759-3f68-4989-a847-a239062b34fc","tierSummary":"$225K – $260K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"2e1b16b7-f939-4832-9ff6-af81eb8cc0f7","summary":"$225K – $260K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":225000,"maxValue":260000},{"id":"61fd6809-404b-4abd-bd91-a74c70f8f433","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"40e503d6-c957-4b4b-9112-f873cb03d004","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":225000,"maxValue":260000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"68a3ac78-d810-4d85-aa00-784f9dd2ea95","title":"Sr. Software Engineer II - Full Stack","department":"Software Engineering","team":"Software Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Palo Alto Office (Hybrid)","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-18T22:04:43.175+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Palo Alto"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/allocate/68a3ac78-d810-4d85-aa00-784f9dd2ea95","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/allocate/68a3ac78-d810-4d85-aa00-784f9dd2ea95/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>About Allocate</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Allocate is building the operating system for private markets. Wealth advisors and their clients use the platform to access, transact in, and manage private market investments. The platform supports 350+ advisory firms and 1,500+ GP relationships, with $ 5B+ in assets on the platform.</p><h1><strong>About The Role</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Allocate is building the operating system for private markets, and this role sits at the center of the product. As a Senior Full Stack Engineer, you will ship features end to end, from Postgres schema and C# APIs through to the Vue and TypeScript interfaces that advisors and their clients use every day to discover, model, transact in, and manage private market investments.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">There is a lot for us to build, and we need an engineer with a genuinely broad skill set who can jump in and help lay the technical foundation for the company's future. You will work in a small, independent, cross-functional squad with real autonomy over what gets built and how, delivering critical features across both our client-facing and admin portals.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are an AI-first engineering organization. Our engineers treat AI coding tools as a core part of the daily workflow, from agentic development through code review, and we expect everyone here to push the boundaries of what those tools can do. We are equally serious about keeping a human in the loop. Engineers own every line that ships, review AI-generated work with the same rigor they would apply to a colleague’s pull request, and stay accountable for the correctness, security, and maintainability of what reaches our clients. The tools accelerate the work; the engineering judgment is still yours.</p><h1><strong>What You’ll Own</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Frontend &amp; Client Experience</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">● Build rich but simple user experiences for new products using Vue.js and TypeScript, from first prototype through production.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">● Partner with product and design to iterate on flows and user experience, then translate them into interfaces that hold up under real advisor workflows.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">● Deliver frontend software that is correct, stable, and security compliant across both the client and admin portals.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Backend, APIs &amp; Data</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">● Design and implement new features and endpoints in our C#/.NET backend APIs.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">● Design and implement the schema changes those features require, with performance in mind: knowing when an index earns its keep, and on which fields.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">● Build high-quality, scalable, testable code that drives engineering maturity and efficiency across the stack.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>AI-First Delivery</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">● Own features end to end as part of an independent, cross-functional squad in an Agile development environment.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">● Use AI coding tools such as Claude Code, Cursor, or Codex as a primary part of your workflow, not an occasional assist.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">● Evaluate emerging tools and agentic workflows continuously, and bring what works back to the rest of engineering.</p><h1><strong>What Success Looks Like</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Within your first 90 days, you have shipped production features that span schema, API, and UI without needing a handoff at the boundary.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Your work is correct, stable, and security compliant on the first pass, so issues are caught in review, not by clients.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• You operate autonomously: you take ambiguous problems, scope them, and drive them to a shipped outcome without supervision.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• You measurably raise the team's AI-assisted development bar, with faster cycle times and repeatable patterns other engineers adopt.</p><h1><strong>Who You Are</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• 5–10 years of experience building web applications, including 5+ years of object-oriented software engineering (C#, Java, or similar).</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• 3+ years of C# experience and 2+ years developing REST APIs.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• 3+ years with the Vue.js front-end framework and 1+ years with TypeScript.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• 5+ years with SQL-based databases (Postgres ideally), including the ability to design a schema that results in a performant application.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• A track record of delivering frontend software that is correct, stable, and security compliant, with strong attention to detail and a feel for what makes good user experience.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• An AI-first development mindset: real experience shipping production code with AI agents using tools like Claude Code, Cursor, or Codex, plus informed opinions on where those tools excel and where they fall short.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Basic understanding of common AWS services (S3, CloudFront, ECS/EKS) and how to apply them to business problems.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Proficiency with Git and the ability to work in a Git-based environment with standard work management tooling.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Autonomy and ownership: you can work effectively without supervision.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Entrepreneurial spirit: self-directed, innovative, biased toward action, and comfortable in ambiguity and even failure.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, a similar technical field of study, or an equivalent amount of real-world experience.</p><h1><strong>Nice to Have</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://ASP.NET\">ASP.NET</a> Web API development experience, plus familiarity with ORM concepts (Dapper, Entity Framework) and FluentMigrator.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Experience with agentic workflows such as running async coding agents, MCP integrations, or custom tooling around LLMs.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Docker and Docker Compose experience, and familiarity with CI pipelines.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• DevOps experience (Terraform, AWS, ECS/EKS).</p><h1><strong>Essential Values &amp; Culture</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• <strong>Providing our clients with a world-class experience is our number one priority. </strong>We obsessively search for ways to improve the experience for our clients and partners. This requires extraordinary response times, proactivity, and ensuring that everything we do, from product strategy to offline communications, reflects a top-tier client experience.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• <strong>Challenge convention:</strong> Instead of detailing all the reasons why an idea may not work, we constantly question things to determine how a viable idea may be put into motion.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• <strong>Commitment to continuous improvement:</strong> We find ways to personally scale each day by pushing ourselves up the learning curve.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• <strong>Meritocracy, not politics: </strong>We place the utmost value on results and rewards through merit, not reward actions driven by political agendas or behavior.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• <strong>Civil Discourse is embraced: </strong>We believe open, intellectually curious conversations are required to consistently arrive at the best decisions. Respect is paramount in our dealings with one another, but our mission is always to get the right answer collectively, not to be right.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• <strong>Embrace technological change:</strong> We adopt tools and techniques that make us faster, smarter, and better. We stay open to innovation, especially around AI and automation, and drop outdated methods without hesitation. This includes actively integrating AI-assisted tools into your daily workflow and staying current as the landscape evolves. Complacency kills progress, and we value adaptability and curiosity.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Additional Details</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Hybrid (3 days/week) in Palo Alto</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Travel may be required for company offsites</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Broadband internet connection required</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Location: All I-9 eligible candidates will be considered</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Salary: <strong>$145,000 – $175,000 </strong>base, with bonus and equity eligibility</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Benefits: Medical, dental, and vision; 401(k); and responsible vacation time (PTO)</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Employment: Full-time</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>The base pay offered will be determined based on the candidate's experience, location, skills, training, certifications, education, internal equity, and market data. Total compensation may also include a discretionary performance-based bonus. We do not anticipate that candidates hired will begin at the top of the range, though this may occur on a case-by-case basis.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT ALLOCATE\n\nAllocate is building the operating system for private markets. Wealth advisors and their clients use the platform to access, transact in, and manage private market investments. The platform supports 350+ advisory firms and 1,500+ GP relationships, with $ 5B+ in assets on the platform.\n\n\nABOUT THE ROLE\n\nAllocate is building the operating system for private markets, and this role sits at the center of the product. As a Senior Full Stack Engineer, you will ship features end to end, from Postgres schema and C# APIs through to the Vue and TypeScript interfaces that advisors and their clients use every day to discover, model, transact in, and manage private market investments.\n\nThere is a lot for us to build, and we need an engineer with a genuinely broad skill set who can jump in and help lay the technical foundation for the company's future. You will work in a small, independent, cross-functional squad with real autonomy over what gets built and how, delivering critical features across both our client-facing and admin portals.\n\nWe are an AI-first engineering organization. Our engineers treat AI coding tools as a core part of the daily workflow, from agentic development through code review, and we expect everyone here to push the boundaries of what those tools can do. We are equally serious about keeping a human in the loop. Engineers own every line that ships, review AI-generated work with the same rigor they would apply to a colleague’s pull request, and stay accountable for the correctness, security, and maintainability of what reaches our clients. The tools accelerate the work; the engineering judgment is still yours.\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL OWN\n\nFrontend & Client Experience\n\n● Build rich but simple user experiences for new products using Vue.js and TypeScript, from first prototype through production.\n\n● Partner with product and design to iterate on flows and user experience, then translate them into interfaces that hold up under real advisor workflows.\n\n● Deliver frontend software that is correct, stable, and security compliant across both the client and admin portals.\n\nBackend, APIs & Data\n\n● Design and implement new features and endpoints in our C#/.NET backend APIs.\n\n● Design and implement the schema changes those features require, with performance in mind: knowing when an index earns its keep, and on which fields.\n\n● Build high-quality, scalable, testable code that drives engineering maturity and efficiency across the stack.\n\nAI-First Delivery\n\n● Own features end to end as part of an independent, cross-functional squad in an Agile development environment.\n\n● Use AI coding tools such as Claude Code, Cursor, or Codex as a primary part of your workflow, not an occasional assist.\n\n● Evaluate emerging tools and agentic workflows continuously, and bring what works back to the rest of engineering.\n\n\nWHAT SUCCESS LOOKS LIKE\n\n• Within your first 90 days, you have shipped production features that span schema, API, and UI without needing a handoff at the boundary.\n\n• Your work is correct, stable, and security compliant on the first pass, so issues are caught in review, not by clients.\n\n• You operate autonomously: you take ambiguous problems, scope them, and drive them to a shipped outcome without supervision.\n\n• You measurably raise the team's AI-assisted development bar, with faster cycle times and repeatable patterns other engineers adopt.\n\n\nWHO YOU ARE\n\n• 5–10 years of experience building web applications, including 5+ years of object-oriented software engineering (C#, Java, or similar).\n\n• 3+ years of C# experience and 2+ years developing REST APIs.\n\n• 3+ years with the Vue.js front-end framework and 1+ years with TypeScript.\n\n• 5+ years with SQL-based databases (Postgres ideally), including the ability to design a schema that results in a performant application.\n\n• A track record of delivering frontend software that is correct, stable, and security compliant, with strong attention to detail and a feel for what makes good user experience.\n\n• An AI-first development mindset: real experience shipping production code with AI agents using tools like Claude Code, Cursor, or Codex, plus informed opinions on where those tools excel and where they fall short.\n\n• Basic understanding of common AWS services (S3, CloudFront, ECS/EKS) and how to apply them to business problems.\n\n• Proficiency with Git and the ability to work in a Git-based environment with standard work management tooling.\n\n• Autonomy and ownership: you can work effectively without supervision.\n\n• Entrepreneurial spirit: self-directed, innovative, biased toward action, and comfortable in ambiguity and even failure.\n\n• Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, a similar technical field of study, or an equivalent amount of real-world experience.\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n• ASP.NET http://ASP.NET Web API development experience, plus familiarity with ORM concepts (Dapper, Entity Framework) and FluentMigrator.\n\n• Experience with agentic workflows such as running async coding agents, MCP integrations, or custom tooling around LLMs.\n\n• Docker and Docker Compose experience, and familiarity with CI pipelines.\n\n• DevOps experience (Terraform, AWS, ECS/EKS).\n\n\nESSENTIAL VALUES & CULTURE\n\n• Providing our clients with a world-class experience is our number one priority. We obsessively search for ways to improve the experience for our clients and partners. This requires extraordinary response times, proactivity, and ensuring that everything we do, from product strategy to offline communications, reflects a top-tier client experience.\n\n• Challenge convention: Instead of detailing all the reasons why an idea may not work, we constantly question things to determine how a viable idea may be put into motion.\n\n• Commitment to continuous improvement: We find ways to personally scale each day by pushing ourselves up the learning curve.\n\n• Meritocracy, not politics: We place the utmost value on results and rewards through merit, not reward actions driven by political agendas or behavior.\n\n• Civil Discourse is embraced: We believe open, intellectually curious conversations are required to consistently arrive at the best decisions. Respect is paramount in our dealings with one another, but our mission is always to get the right answer collectively, not to be right.\n\n• Embrace technological change: We adopt tools and techniques that make us faster, smarter, and better. We stay open to innovation, especially around AI and automation, and drop outdated methods without hesitation. This includes actively integrating AI-assisted tools into your daily workflow and staying current as the landscape evolves. Complacency kills progress, and we value adaptability and curiosity.\n\n\n\n\nADDITIONAL DETAILS\n\n• Hybrid (3 days/week) in Palo Alto\n\n• Travel may be required for company offsites\n\n• Broadband internet connection required\n\n• Location: All I-9 eligible candidates will be considered\n\n• Salary: $145,000 – $175,000 base, with bonus and equity eligibility\n\n• Benefits: Medical, dental, and vision; 401(k); and responsible vacation time (PTO)\n\n• Employment: Full-time\n\n\n\nThe base pay offered will be determined based on the candidate's experience, location, skills, training, certifications, education, internal equity, and market data. Total compensation may also include a discretionary performance-based bonus. We do not anticipate that candidates hired will begin at the top of the range, though this may occur on a case-by-case basis.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$145K – $175K","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$145K - $175K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"35068e2b-0524-4ea3-a4cf-3063432ba9d5","tierSummary":"$145K – $175K","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"70ec7b58-3227-45b9-a40b-cc5b76006b78","summary":"$145K – $175K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":145000,"maxValue":175000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":145000,"maxValue":175000}]}},{"id":"ac0f7123-32e6-42ce-9cfb-1d2b2f5cf5d8","title":"Sales Operations Manager","department":"Relationship Management","team":"Relationship Management","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Palo Alto Office (Hybrid)","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"New York (Hybrid)","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York"}}}],"publishedAt":"2026-08-27T16:38:29.873+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Palo Alto"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/allocate/ac0f7123-32e6-42ce-9cfb-1d2b2f5cf5d8","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/allocate/ac0f7123-32e6-42ce-9cfb-1d2b2f5cf5d8/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>About Allocate</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Allocate is building the operating system for private markets — wealth advisors and their clients use the platform to access, transact in, and manage private market investments. The platform supports 350+ advisory firms and 1,500+ GP relationships, with $ 5B+ in assets on the platform.</p><h1><strong>About The Role</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As the Relationship Management organization scales into two distinct motions — Capital Formation &amp; Wealth Advisory Solutions— Allocate needs a single owner for the operating rigor that keeps both motions accountable, forecastable, and clean. This role is the CRO's right hand on data and process: you build the systems that turn activity into a trustworthy number.</p><h1><strong>What You’ll Own</strong></h1><h2><strong>Pipeline Tracking &amp; Forecasting</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define and maintain pipeline stage gates for each sales and product motion (advisory vs. structured enterprise pursuit), including renewals and expansion</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track pipeline creation, velocity, and conversion by stage, rep, and surface area; flag stalled or at-risk opportunities before they become forecast misses</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and run forecasting by product/motion (Capital Formation &amp; Advisory vs. Platform Sales), rolling up to a company forecast and ARR goals</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own forecast cadence and accuracy tracking against actuals — the source of truth the CRO and board rely on</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Activity &amp; Meeting Reporting</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Report call and meeting volume/quality by rep and by team</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Surface leading-indicator activity metrics to the CRO, CXO, and CEO ahead of pipeline reviews</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Territory &amp; Coverage Reporting</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build territory/account coverage reports across GPs, family offices, and advisors (Capital Formation) and enterprise buying groups (RIAs)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with the CRO on account ownership assignment and overlap resolution, ensuring single ownership across existing and greenfield accounts</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide white-glove client experience and business continuity support for RM changes by aligning Associate Relationship Managers with each account</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support Relationship Managers with strategic list pulls and targeting for marketing events and campaigns</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Aging &amp; Hygiene</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Run aging reports on open opportunities, stalled deals, active onboarding, and overdue next steps</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain Salesforce hygiene: data completeness, required-field enforcement, lead dedup across both teams, and ownership-field accuracy</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Revenue Operating System</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help redefine the RM process end-to-end: stage definitions, exit criteria, and instrumented funnel metrics</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive action items from the biweekly cross-team pipeline review cadence</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Finance on revenue recognition inputs and unit economics data &amp; prepare board- and investor-ready reports for the CEO</p></li></ul><h1><strong>What Success Looks Like</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Forecast accuracy improves quarter over quarter, by product/motion and in aggregate</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CRM data is clean by default, no manual scrubbing before a board meeting</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Pipeline reviews run on real, current data with zero “let me check and get back to you”</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Account ownership is unambiguous</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">RMs spend less time on reporting, more time selling. This role absorbs that overhead.</p></li></ul><h1><strong>Who You Are</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years in sales ops / revenue ops, ideally in a company running multiple distinct sales motions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep Salesforce fluency. Not just reports and dashboards but using it to create real operational leverage</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable being the source of truth on numbers that go to the CEO and board</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Detail-oriented on hygiene, but able to zoom out to forecasting and process design</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in fintech, wealth management, or private markets is a plus, not a requirement</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Essential Values &amp; Culture</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Providing our clients with a world-class experience is our number one priority. </strong>We obsessively search for ways to improve the experience for our clients and partners. This requires extraordinary response times, proactivity, and ensuring that everything we do — from product strategy to offline communications — reflects a top-tier client experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Challenge convention:</strong> Instead of detailing all the reasons why an idea may not work, we constantly question things to determine how a viable idea may be put into motion.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Commitment to continuous improvement:</strong> We find ways to personally scale each day by pushing ourselves up the learning curve.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Meritocracy, not politics: </strong>We place the utmost value on results and rewards through merit, not reward actions driven by political agendas or behavior.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Civil Discourse is embraced: </strong>We believe open, intellectually curious conversations are required to consistently arrive at the best decisions. Respect is paramount in our dealings with one another, but our mission is always to get the right answer collectively, not to be right.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Embrace technological change:</strong> We adopt tools and techniques that make us faster, smarter, and better. We stay open to innovation, especially around AI and automation, and drop outdated methods without hesitation. This includes actively integrating AI-assisted tools into your daily workflow and staying current as the landscape evolves. Complacency kills progress — we value adaptability and curiosity.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Additional Details</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fully Hybrid Position</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Travel may be required for company offsites</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Broadband internet connection required</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Location: All I-9 eligible candidates will be considered</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Salary: $150,000+ base, with bonus and equity eligibility</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Benefits: Medical, dental, and vision; 401(k); and responsible vacation time (PTO)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Employment: Full-time</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>The base pay offered will be determined based on the candidate's experience, location, skills, training, certifications, education, internal equity, and market data. Total compensation may also include a discretionary performance-based bonus. We do not anticipate that candidates hired will begin at the top of the range, though this may occur on a case-by-case basis.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT ALLOCATE\n\nAllocate is building the operating system for private markets — wealth advisors and their clients use the platform to access, transact in, and manage private market investments. The platform supports 350+ advisory firms and 1,500+ GP relationships, with $ 5B+ in assets on the platform.\n\n\nABOUT THE ROLE\n\nAs the Relationship Management organization scales into two distinct motions — Capital Formation & Wealth Advisory Solutions— Allocate needs a single owner for the operating rigor that keeps both motions accountable, forecastable, and clean. This role is the CRO's right hand on data and process: you build the systems that turn activity into a trustworthy number.\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL OWN\n\n\nPIPELINE TRACKING & FORECASTING\n\n - Define and maintain pipeline stage gates for each sales and product motion (advisory vs. structured enterprise pursuit), including renewals and expansion\n\n - Track pipeline creation, velocity, and conversion by stage, rep, and surface area; flag stalled or at-risk opportunities before they become forecast misses\n\n - Build and run forecasting by product/motion (Capital Formation & Advisory vs. Platform Sales), rolling up to a company forecast and ARR goals\n\n - Own forecast cadence and accuracy tracking against actuals — the source of truth the CRO and board rely on\n\n\nACTIVITY & MEETING REPORTING\n\n - Report call and meeting volume/quality by rep and by team\n\n - Surface leading-indicator activity metrics to the CRO, CXO, and CEO ahead of pipeline reviews\n\n\nTERRITORY & COVERAGE REPORTING\n\n - Build territory/account coverage reports across GPs, family offices, and advisors (Capital Formation) and enterprise buying groups (RIAs)\n\n - Partner with the CRO on account ownership assignment and overlap resolution, ensuring single ownership across existing and greenfield accounts\n\n - Provide white-glove client experience and business continuity support for RM changes by aligning Associate Relationship Managers with each account\n\n - Support Relationship Managers with strategic list pulls and targeting for marketing events and campaigns\n\nAging & Hygiene\n\n - Run aging reports on open opportunities, stalled deals, active onboarding, and overdue next steps\n\n - Maintain Salesforce hygiene: data completeness, required-field enforcement, lead dedup across both teams, and ownership-field accuracy\n\n\nREVENUE OPERATING SYSTEM\n\n - Help redefine the RM process end-to-end: stage definitions, exit criteria, and instrumented funnel metrics\n\n - Drive action items from the biweekly cross-team pipeline review cadence\n\n - Partner with Finance on revenue recognition inputs and unit economics data & prepare board- and investor-ready reports for the CEO\n\n\nWHAT SUCCESS LOOKS LIKE\n\n - Forecast accuracy improves quarter over quarter, by product/motion and in aggregate\n\n - CRM data is clean by default, no manual scrubbing before a board meeting\n\n - Pipeline reviews run on real, current data with zero “let me check and get back to you”\n\n - Account ownership is unambiguous\n\n - RMs spend less time on reporting, more time selling. This role absorbs that overhead.\n\n\nWHO YOU ARE\n\n - 5+ years in sales ops / revenue ops, ideally in a company running multiple distinct sales motions\n\n - Deep Salesforce fluency. Not just reports and dashboards but using it to create real operational leverage\n\n - Comfortable being the source of truth on numbers that go to the CEO and board\n\n - Detail-oriented on hygiene, but able to zoom out to forecasting and process design\n\n - Experience in fintech, wealth management, or private markets is a plus, not a requirement\n\n\n\n\nESSENTIAL VALUES & CULTURE\n\n - Providing our clients with a world-class experience is our number one priority. We obsessively search for ways to improve the experience for our clients and partners. This requires extraordinary response times, proactivity, and ensuring that everything we do — from product strategy to offline communications — reflects a top-tier client experience.\n\n - Challenge convention: Instead of detailing all the reasons why an idea may not work, we constantly question things to determine how a viable idea may be put into motion.\n\n - Commitment to continuous improvement: We find ways to personally scale each day by pushing ourselves up the learning curve.\n\n - Meritocracy, not politics: We place the utmost value on results and rewards through merit, not reward actions driven by political agendas or behavior.\n\n - Civil Discourse is embraced: We believe open, intellectually curious conversations are required to consistently arrive at the best decisions. Respect is paramount in our dealings with one another, but our mission is always to get the right answer collectively, not to be right.\n\n - Embrace technological change: We adopt tools and techniques that make us faster, smarter, and better. We stay open to innovation, especially around AI and automation, and drop outdated methods without hesitation. This includes actively integrating AI-assisted tools into your daily workflow and staying current as the landscape evolves. Complacency kills progress — we value adaptability and curiosity.\n\n\n\n\nADDITIONAL DETAILS\n\n - Fully Hybrid Position\n\n - Travel may be required for company offsites\n\n - Broadband internet connection required\n\n - Location: All I-9 eligible candidates will be considered\n\n - Salary: $150,000+ base, with bonus and equity eligibility\n\n - Benefits: Medical, dental, and vision; 401(k); and responsible vacation time (PTO)\n\n - Employment: Full-time\n\n\n\nThe base pay offered will be determined based on the candidate's experience, location, skills, training, certifications, education, internal equity, and market data. Total compensation may also include a discretionary performance-based bonus. We do not anticipate that candidates hired will begin at the top of the range, though this may occur on a case-by-case basis.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$150K – $180K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$150K - $180K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"994014db-fddf-4460-bd19-e0ebe04c651b","tierSummary":"$150K – $180K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"50e0a48c-85c4-43e4-9fdc-ad41269fbfe2","summary":"$150K – $180K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":150000,"maxValue":180000},{"id":"36645fd3-54fe-4089-a9b3-c0cae0453f75","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"888bf428-7249-4c7f-9572-1dead425a976","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":150000,"maxValue":180000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"07d9aa8c-67e6-48e0-a7f9-e1b4440f42f9","title":"Fund Operations Analyst","department":"Fund Finance","team":"Fund Finance","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York (Hybrid)","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"Palo Alto Office (Hybrid)","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Palo Alto"}}}],"publishedAt":"2026-09-01T16:21:47.445+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/allocate/07d9aa8c-67e6-48e0-a7f9-e1b4440f42f9","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/allocate/07d9aa8c-67e6-48e0-a7f9-e1b4440f42f9/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Allocate</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Allocate is building the operating system for private markets — wealth advisors and their clients use the platform to access, transact in, and manage private market investments. The platform supports 350+ advisory firms and 1,500+ GP relationships, with $5B+ in assets on the platform.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About The Role</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Fund Operations Analyst, you will run the daily execution engine behind the 150+ funds on the Allocate platform. Capital call notices, wires and transfers, credit facility drawdowns, payment matching, expense reconciliation, and the records that everything else depends on.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As Allocate scales, the fund count on the platform is growing quickly, and we need to keep automating our processes to keep pace. You will learn the operational process, then work with the team and spearhead the efforts on how we can  automate our workflows. This is a hands-on execution role with a build mandate attached, and you will be measured on two things. Did the work deliver a superb client experience, accurate and on time every time, and can the same team handle more funds this quarter than it could last quarter.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What You'll Own</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will work day to day alongside our Allocate Fund Finance team, splitting coverage across the fund portfolio, and report directly to the Head of Feeder Operations. You will also partner closely with our client service team, third-party fund administrators, audit and tax teams.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Fund Lifecycle Operations</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">•     Prepare capital call notices across the fund portfolio and route them for review and approval.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">•     Set up wires and transfers across our banking platforms, including capital call fundings and distributions to limited and general partners.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">•     Reconcile daily partner activity across bank accounts, flag anything that does not tie, and support quarterly cash queries from the fund administrator and auditors.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">•     Own fund expense reconciliation. Code and allocate incoming invoices to the correct fund, series, and period, maintain and true up accruals, reconcile expenses against bank activity and the administrator’s books, and carry clean support into quarterly review and the annual audit.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">•     Prepare credit facility drawdowns ahead of capital call deadlines, track repayments and outstanding balances, and pull together quarterly compliance reporting.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">•     Own the core operational trackers covering investment activity, capital call payments, distributions, credit facilities, tax document status, and investor commitment records.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">•     Review quarterly fund financials against source workpapers and tie the statements to the underlying schedules before anything goes out.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">•     Assist in opening bank and brokerage accounts for new funds, including compiling the required entity documentation and maintaining account records.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Automation and Process</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">•     Document every workflow you touch and create new processes for those that don’t currently exist. If it is not written down, it cannot be audited, operationalized, improved, or automated.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">•    Partner with Product and Engineering to push repeatable operational logic into the platform rather than keeping it in spreadsheets.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">•     Build the automation. Templated notice generation, rules-based payment matching, invoice intake and expense allocation, self-updating accrual roll forwards, scheduled reconciliations, automatic file routing, and alerting on exceptions instead of manual daily checks.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">•     Replace manual tracker updates with queries and dashboards pulled from the source systems.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What Success Looks Like</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">•     Capital calls, distributions, and wires go out accurately and on deadline, with no client-visible errors.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">•     Expense reconciliation closes on schedule each period, with documented support that the administrator and auditors accept without a round of follow-up questions.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">•     Manual hours come out of the core workflows every quarter, measured against the tasks you have automated or eliminated.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">•     The fund count grows without a matching increase in operational headcount or cycle time.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Who You Are</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">•     1 to 3 years of experience in fund operations, fund administration, treasury, audit, or a related finance function, with a working understanding of private fund mechanics. Capital calls, distributions, fund expenses, capital accounts, and investor reporting.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">•     Real reconciliation experience, and precision under deadline pressure. You have owned an expense or cash reconciliation before, you are comfortable explaining a variance to a reviewer, and you know that wire cutoffs and capital call dates do not move.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">•     Process minded by instinct, and already using AI to take repetitive work off your plate. You write things down, you notice when the same problem shows up twice, and you fix the cause instead of the instance.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">•     Strong communicator. You coordinate clearly with fund administrators, banks, auditors, and internal teams, and you keep people updated without being asked.</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Growth-oriented and energized by a scaling environment. You want to grow with the firm and take on more ownership as the fund count and team expand.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Nice to Have</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">•     Experience working alongside a third-party fund administrator, reviewing and challenging their output rather than producing it yourself.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">•     Treasury or payment operations background. Working in a bank portal with dual approval workflows, wire cutoffs, and payment controls.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">•     Time in an early-stage or high-growth environment where the process did not exist yet and you had to build it.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Essential Values &amp; Culture</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">•     Providing our clients with a world-class experience is our number one priority. We obsessively search for ways to improve the experience for our clients and partners. This requires extraordinary response times, proactivity, and ensuring that everything we do — from product strategy to offline communications — reflects a top-tier client experience.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">•     Challenge convention: Instead of detailing all the reasons why an idea may not work, we constantly question things to determine how a viable idea may be put into motion.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">•     Commitment to continuous improvement: We find ways to personally scale each day by pushing ourselves up the learning curve.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">•     Meritocracy, not politics: We place the utmost value on results and rewards through merit, not reward actions driven by political agendas or behavior.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">•     Civil Discourse is embraced: We believe open, intellectually curious conversations are required to consistently arrive at the best decisions. Respect is paramount in our dealings with one another, but our mission is always to get the right answer collectively, not to be right.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">•     Embrace technological change: We adopt tools and techniques that make us faster, smarter, and better. We stay open to innovation, especially around AI and automation, and drop outdated methods without hesitation. This includes actively integrating AI-assisted tools into your daily workflow and staying current as the landscape evolves. Complacency kills progress — we value adaptability and curiosity.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Additional Details</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">•     Fully Hybrid Position</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">•     Travel may be required for company offsites</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">•     Broadband internet connection required</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">•     Location: All I-9 eligible candidates will be considered</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">•     Salary: $85,000 – $100,000 base, with bonus and equity eligibility</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">•     Benefits: Medical, dental, and vision; 401(k); and responsible vacation time (PTO)</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">•     Employment: Full-time</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The base pay offered will be determined based on the candidate’s experience, location, skills, training, certifications, education, internal equity, and market data. Total compensation may also include a discretionary performance-based bonus. We do not anticipate that candidates hired will begin at the top of the range, though this may occur on a case-by-case basis.</p>","descriptionPlain":"About Allocate\n\nAllocate is building the operating system for private markets — wealth advisors and their clients use the platform to access, transact in, and manage private market investments. The platform supports 350+ advisory firms and 1,500+ GP relationships, with $5B+ in assets on the platform.\n\nAbout The Role\n\nAs a Fund Operations Analyst, you will run the daily execution engine behind the 150+ funds on the Allocate platform. Capital call notices, wires and transfers, credit facility drawdowns, payment matching, expense reconciliation, and the records that everything else depends on.\n\nAs Allocate scales, the fund count on the platform is growing quickly, and we need to keep automating our processes to keep pace. You will learn the operational process, then work with the team and spearhead the efforts on how we can  automate our workflows. This is a hands-on execution role with a build mandate attached, and you will be measured on two things. Did the work deliver a superb client experience, accurate and on time every time, and can the same team handle more funds this quarter than it could last quarter.\n\nWhat You'll Own\n\nYou will work day to day alongside our Allocate Fund Finance team, splitting coverage across the fund portfolio, and report directly to the Head of Feeder Operations. You will also partner closely with our client service team, third-party fund administrators, audit and tax teams.\n\nFund Lifecycle Operations\n\n•     Prepare capital call notices across the fund portfolio and route them for review and approval.\n\n•     Set up wires and transfers across our banking platforms, including capital call fundings and distributions to limited and general partners.\n\n•     Reconcile daily partner activity across bank accounts, flag anything that does not tie, and support quarterly cash queries from the fund administrator and auditors.\n\n•     Own fund expense reconciliation. Code and allocate incoming invoices to the correct fund, series, and period, maintain and true up accruals, reconcile expenses against bank activity and the administrator’s books, and carry clean support into quarterly review and the annual audit.\n\n•     Prepare credit facility drawdowns ahead of capital call deadlines, track repayments and outstanding balances, and pull together quarterly compliance reporting.\n\n•     Own the core operational trackers covering investment activity, capital call payments, distributions, credit facilities, tax document status, and investor commitment records.\n\n•     Review quarterly fund financials against source workpapers and tie the statements to the underlying schedules before anything goes out.\n\n•     Assist in opening bank and brokerage accounts for new funds, including compiling the required entity documentation and maintaining account records.\n\nAutomation and Process\n\n•     Document every workflow you touch and create new processes for those that don’t currently exist. If it is not written down, it cannot be audited, operationalized, improved, or automated.\n\n•    Partner with Product and Engineering to push repeatable operational logic into the platform rather than keeping it in spreadsheets.\n\n•     Build the automation. Templated notice generation, rules-based payment matching, invoice intake and expense allocation, self-updating accrual roll forwards, scheduled reconciliations, automatic file routing, and alerting on exceptions instead of manual daily checks.\n\n•     Replace manual tracker updates with queries and dashboards pulled from the source systems.\n\nWhat Success Looks Like\n\n•     Capital calls, distributions, and wires go out accurately and on deadline, with no client-visible errors.\n\n•     Expense reconciliation closes on schedule each period, with documented support that the administrator and auditors accept without a round of follow-up questions.\n\n•     Manual hours come out of the core workflows every quarter, measured against the tasks you have automated or eliminated.\n\n•     The fund count grows without a matching increase in operational headcount or cycle time.\n\nWho You Are\n\n•     1 to 3 years of experience in fund operations, fund administration, treasury, audit, or a related finance function, with a working understanding of private fund mechanics. Capital calls, distributions, fund expenses, capital accounts, and investor reporting.\n\n•     Real reconciliation experience, and precision under deadline pressure. You have owned an expense or cash reconciliation before, you are comfortable explaining a variance to a reviewer, and you know that wire cutoffs and capital call dates do not move.\n\n•     Process minded by instinct, and already using AI to take repetitive work off your plate. You write things down, you notice when the same problem shows up twice, and you fix the cause instead of the instance.\n\n•     Strong communicator. You coordinate clearly with fund administrators, banks, auditors, and internal teams, and you keep people updated without being asked.\n\n - Growth-oriented and energized by a scaling environment. You want to grow with the firm and take on more ownership as the fund count and team expand.\n\nNice to Have\n\n•     Experience working alongside a third-party fund administrator, reviewing and challenging their output rather than producing it yourself.\n\n•     Treasury or payment operations background. Working in a bank portal with dual approval workflows, wire cutoffs, and payment controls.\n\n•     Time in an early-stage or high-growth environment where the process did not exist yet and you had to build it.\n\nEssential Values & Culture\n\n•     Providing our clients with a world-class experience is our number one priority. We obsessively search for ways to improve the experience for our clients and partners. This requires extraordinary response times, proactivity, and ensuring that everything we do — from product strategy to offline communications — reflects a top-tier client experience.\n\n•     Challenge convention: Instead of detailing all the reasons why an idea may not work, we constantly question things to determine how a viable idea may be put into motion.\n\n•     Commitment to continuous improvement: We find ways to personally scale each day by pushing ourselves up the learning curve.\n\n•     Meritocracy, not politics: We place the utmost value on results and rewards through merit, not reward actions driven by political agendas or behavior.\n\n•     Civil Discourse is embraced: We believe open, intellectually curious conversations are required to consistently arrive at the best decisions. Respect is paramount in our dealings with one another, but our mission is always to get the right answer collectively, not to be right.\n\n•     Embrace technological change: We adopt tools and techniques that make us faster, smarter, and better. We stay open to innovation, especially around AI and automation, and drop outdated methods without hesitation. This includes actively integrating AI-assisted tools into your daily workflow and staying current as the landscape evolves. Complacency kills progress — we value adaptability and curiosity.\n\nAdditional Details\n\n•     Fully Hybrid Position\n\n•     Travel may be required for company offsites\n\n•     Broadband internet connection required\n\n•     Location: All I-9 eligible candidates will be considered\n\n•     Salary: $85,000 – $100,000 base, with bonus and equity eligibility\n\n•     Benefits: Medical, dental, and vision; 401(k); and responsible vacation time (PTO)\n\n•     Employment: Full-time\n\n\n\nThe base pay offered will be determined based on the candidate’s experience, location, skills, training, certifications, education, internal equity, and market data. Total compensation may also include a discretionary performance-based bonus. We do not anticipate that candidates hired will begin at the top of the range, though this may occur on a case-by-case basis.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$85K – $100K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$85K - $100K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"d68aa87c-3f73-410f-b91e-15156faaa85e","tierSummary":"$85K – $100K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"a47c64a3-a5f1-4cb2-bb3f-95d4f26c3938","summary":"$85K – $100K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":85000,"maxValue":100000},{"id":"61b17a1c-2503-4296-8af3-ee0944228880","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"d82b6478-f550-4116-aabe-41cadf27b2a4","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":85000,"maxValue":100000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}}],"apiVersion":"1"}